{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786124673627,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_uMe9zvLiVCm5Bynr3Pb89621","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Convergence\n3: description: Stop condition algorithms, quality guards, and recovery strategies for the autonomous deep review loop.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review convergence detection\"\n6:   - \"severity weighted stop ratio\"\n7:   - \"legal stop gate bundle\"\n8:   - \"review stuck detection\"\n9:   - \"composite convergence vote\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.0.22\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review Convergence\n16: \n17: Stop condition algorithms, quality guards, and stuck recovery for the deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: Convergence detection determines when the autonomous review loop should stop iterating. After every iteration the orchestrator evaluates three possible outcomes:\n26: \n27: | Outcome | Meaning |\n28: |---------|---------|\n29: | **CONTINUE** | More review work is expected to yield meaningful new findings. Dispatch the next iteration. |\n30: | **STOP** | The review has reached saturation. Proceed to synthesis and verdict. |\n31: | **STUCK_RECOVERY** | No progress detected for consecutive iterations. Attempt a recovery strategy before deciding. |\n32: \n33: Convergence is checked **after** each iteration completes and **before** the next iteration is dispatched. The check consumes the full JSONL state history and the current dimension coverage snapshot.\n34: \n35: Release-readiness states are derived alongside convergence:\n36: - `in-progress` while coverage is incomplete or new P0/P1 findings are still appearing\n37: - `converged` once coverage and stabilization pass without new P0/P1 findings\n38: - `release-blocking` whenever unresolved P0 findings remain active\n39: \n40: When the loop stops and enters synthesis, the workflow emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md` from converged review deltas before compiling `review-report.md`. Operators can disable that write with `--no-resource-map`.\n41: \n42: ### When to Use\n43: \n44: - Evaluating whether the autonomous review loop should stop, continue, or recover.\n45: - Tuning convergence thresholds, stuck-recovery cadence, or stabilization windows.\n46: - Debugging a stuck-recovery escalation or a premature STOP vote.\n47: - Auditing the release-readiness classification logic before shipping.\n48: \n49: ### Key Defaults\n50: \n51: | Setting | Value | Purpose |\n52: |---------|-------|---------|\n53: | `maxIterations` | 7 | Hard ceiling on loop iterations |\n54: | `convergenceThreshold` | 0.10 | General convergence sensitivity |\n55: | `rollingStopThreshold` | 0.08 | Rolling-average STOP vote threshold |\n56: | `noProgressThreshold` | 0.05 | Stuck / no-progress classification threshold |\n57: | `stuckThreshold` | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n58: | `minStabilizationPasses` | 1 | Coverage signal requires at least one stabilization pass |\n59: | `compositeStopScore` | 0.60 | Weighted stop-score needed before guard evaluation |\n60: \n61: ### Threshold Semantics and Sibling Parity\n62: \n63: `convergenceThreshold` (default 0.10) compares new severity-weighted findings (P0=10, P1=5, P2=1) against accumulated findings. Lower values demand more iterations and a higher signal threshold before STOP is legal.\n64: \n65: **Not interchangeable with sibling deep-loop skills:**\n66: \n67: | Skill | Default | Signal |\n68: |---|---|---|\n69: | `deep-review` | 0.10 | severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 ratio |\n70: | `deep-research` | 0.05 | newInfoRatio (negative-knowledge emphasis) |\n71: | `deep-ai-council` (proposed) | 0.20 | adjudicator-verdict stability |\n72: \n73: Carrying threshold expectations across siblings will cause unexpected iteration counts. Tune each skill against its own default and its own signal, not by analogy.\n74: \n75: ### Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\n76: \n77: > **STATUS: SPEC ONLY (future implementation).** The override matrix below describes the contract that a future release should apply automatically when the review target involves security-sensitive surfaces. As of v1.9.0.0, the runtime does NOT auto-detect security-sensitivity and does NOT apply these overrides. `requiredClosedFindingReplay` and `requiredFixCompletenessGate` exist in no config / yaml / reducer surface (verified by grep). Operators running a security-sensitive review must manually tighten thresholds via `--convergence` + `--max-iterations` and manually maintain the closed-gate replay table. The contract below stands as the target spec for the next implementation pass. (Provenance for this deferred contract is recorded in this skill's changelog.)\n78: \n79: For review reruns after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads (intended contract, not yet runtime-enforced):\n80: \n81: | Setting | General Default | Security-Sensitive Fix Default |\n82: |---------|-----------------|--------------------------------|\n83: | `minStabilizationPasses` | 1 | 2 |\n84: | `requiredClosedFindingReplay` | false | true for prior P0/P1 and any prior security/path P2 |\n85: | `requiredFixCompletenessGate` | false | true |\n86: \n87: When implemented, STOP must not be legal until the review report contains a closed-gate replay table that marks each prior active or remediated P0/P1 as `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `carried forward`, with file:line or command evidence. Operators today must enforce this rule manually.\n88: \n89: ### Shared Stop Contract\n90: \n91: Every terminal stop and every blocked-stop vote MUST emit the shared stop contract from REQ-001: a named `stopReason` enum plus, when STOP is vetoed, a `blocked_stop` event written to `deep-review-state.jsonl`. There is no nested `legalStop` wrapper on the persisted path. Earlier drafts of this document implied one, and that drift was the source of F009 in the 042 closing audit.\n92: \n93: ### Convergence Modes\n94: \n95: The shared convergence runtime accepts four values. Review legality, security gates, target authority, and verdict derivation remain owned by the review workflow rather than the convergence mode.\n96: \n97: | Mode | Live Behavior |\n98: |------|---------------|\n99: | `default` | Uses normal full-history convergence signals and sends a legal STOP to synthesis and verdict derivation. This is the fallback when no mode is supplied. |\n100: | `off` | Is accepted and persisted, but the shipped review YAML has no `off` decision branch; review therefore follows the same legal-stop and synthesis path as `default`. Use `stopPolicy: \"max-iterations\"` when convergence must remain telemetry-only until the iteration ceiling. |\n101: | `sliding-window` | Is accepted and persisted, but windowed graph-novelty telemetry is research-only in the shared runtime; review therefore retains its ordinary full-history signals, legal-stop gates, and synthesis path. |\n102: | `divergent` | After all review gates pass, translates the eligible `all_dimensions_clean` STOP into a read-only three-seat direction-selection pivot and continues with the selected review direction. |\n103: \n104: #### Divergent Pivot Contract\n105: \n106: Review has one eligible reason: the exact internal reason `all_dimensions_clean` with decision `STOP`. The nine legal-stop gates run before the divergent branch and remain unchanged. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, unrecoverable error, and any blocked security or quality gate therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.\n107: \n108: Each eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n109: \n110: The guarantees are absolute: divergent mode never changes the PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL mapping, never authorizes a fix, and never makes the review target writable. A successful pivot returns to the loop before `phase_synthesis`; verdict computation exists only inside `phase_synthesis`, where active P0 yields FAIL, active P1 yields CONDITIONAL, and no active P0/P1 yields PASS. A failed pivot fails closed to that existing synthesis path.\n111: \n112: Every pivot dispatches three seats, so a run that pivots has proportionally higher model cost and duration than the same run under `default`, `off`, or `sliding-window`. Pivot evidence is isolated under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, including config, append-only state, three seat artifacts, deliberation, and report. This path is distinct from ordinary planning Council artifacts under a spec packet's `ai-council/**` tree.\n113: \n114: #### stopReason Enum\n115: \n116: | `stopReason` | Meaning |\n117: |--------------|---------|\n118: | `converged` | All convergence signals met and legal-stop gates passed. |\n119: | `maxIterationsReached` | Iteration limit hit before convergence. |\n120: | `userPaused` | User requested pause via sentinel. |\n121: | `blockedStop` | Convergence math voted stop but legal-stop gates failed. |\n122: | `stuckRecovery` | Stuck detection triggered recovery. |\n123: | `error` | Unrecoverable error during iteration or reducer flow. |\n124: | `manualStop` | Operator explicitly halted outside the pause sentinel path. |\n125: \n126: #### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n127: \n128: `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n129: \n130: ```json\n131: {\n132:   \"type\": \"event\",\n133:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n134:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n135:   \"run\": 5,\n136:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n137:   \"gateResults\": {\n138:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n139:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n140:       \"pass\": false,\n141:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n142:       \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n143:     },\n144:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n145:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n146:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n147:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n148:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n149:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n150:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n151:   },\n152:   \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n153:   \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n154:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n155:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n156:   \"generation\": 1\n157: }\n158: ```\n159: \n160: - `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n161: - `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n162: - `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n163: - `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.\n164: - When the graph convergence verdict is `STOP_BLOCKED`, fold the graph blocker gate name into `blockedBy` and preserve the structured blocker objects under `graphBlockerDetail`.\n165: \n166: ### Decision Priority\n167: \n168: Checks are evaluated in this order (first match wins):\n169: \n170: 1. **Max iterations** -- hard cap, always checked first.\n171: 2. **All dimensions covered + clean** -- all 4 dimensions covered, no active P0/P1, stabilization passed, gates passed.\n172: 3. **Stuck detection** -- 2+ consecutive no-progress iterations.\n173: 4. **Composite convergence** -- 3-signal weighted vote with threshold 0.60.\n174: 5. **Legal-stop gate bundle** -- review-specific stop gates. If a stop vote fails any gate, persist `stopReason=blockedStop` and continue.\n175: 6. **Default CONTINUE** -- none of the above triggered.\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: ## 2. HARD STOPS\n180: \n181: Hard stops are evaluated first and override all other signals.\n182: \n183: ### Max Iterations Reached\n184: \n185: ```\n186: if len(iterations) >= config.maxIterations:       // default 7\n187:   return { action: \"STOP\", stopReason: \"maxIterationsReached\" }\n188: ```\n189: \n190: The loop stops unconditionally. Synthesis runs with whatever findings exist.\n191: \n192: ### All Dimensions Covered with Stabilization\n193: \n194: ```\n195: if coverage.dimensionCoverage == 1.0 and activeP0 == 0 and activeP1 == 0:\n196:   if stabilizationPasses >= config.coverageAge.minStabilizationPasses:\n197:     if buildReviewLegalStop(state, config, coverage).passed:\n198:       return { action: \"STOP\", stopReason: \"converged\" }\n199: ```\n200: \n201: Triggers when all 4 dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) are covered, no active P0/P1 remains, at least 1 stabilization pass has occurred, and the 5-gate legal-stop bundle passes. If gates fail, the loop records `stopReason=blockedStop` and continues despite full coverage.\n202: \n203: ---\n204: \n205: ## 3. STUCK DETECTION\n206: \n207: Identifies when the review loop makes no meaningful progress across consecutive iterations.\n208: \n209: ```\n210: function countConsecutiveStuck_review(evidenceIterations, noProgressThreshold):\n211:   count = 0\n212:   for i in reversed(evidenceIterations):\n213:     if i.status == \"thought\":   continue    // invisible to stuck counter\n214:     if i.status == \"insight\":   break       // resets stuck counter (genuine progress)\n215:     if i.newFindingsRatio < noProgressThreshold or i.status == \"stuck\":\n216:       count += 1\n217:     else:\n218:       break\n219:   return count\n220: ```\n221: \n222: **Threshold:** `stuckThreshold = 2` consecutive no-progress iterations (using `noProgressThreshold = 0.05`).\n223: \n224: **Status exclusions:**\n225: - `insight`: Resets stuck counter -- a conceptual breakthrough counts as progress even with a low ratio.\n226: - `thought`: Skipped entirely -- analytical iterations produce no evidence to measure.\n227: \n228: When `stuckCount >= stuckThreshold`, the orchestrator invokes the recovery protocol (Section 8) before deciding whether to continue or stop.\n229: \n230: The recovery entry uses `stopReason=stuckRecovery` while the loop is in recovery. If recovery later terminates the run, the terminal record keeps the same shared enum value instead of minting a review-only label.\n231: \n232: ---\n233: \n234: ## 4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE\n235: \n236: Three independent signals each cast a stop/continue vote. Stop when the weighted stop-score meets or exceeds the consensus threshold. The signal set below matches the authoritative 3-signal vote in `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` `step_check_convergence` and the quick-reference convergence table, the 3rd signal is **dimension coverage**, not a standalone novelty ratio.\n237: \n238: | Signal | Weight | Min Iterations | Measures |\n239: |--------|--------|---------------|----------|\n240: | Rolling Average | 0.30 | 2 | Recent severity-weighted finding yield |\n241: | MAD Noise Floor | 0.25 | 3 | Signal vs noise in newFindingsRatio |\n242: | Dimension Coverage | 0.45 | 1 | Configured review dimensions fully covered AND required traceability protocols covered AND `coverage_age >= minStabilizationPasses` |\n243: \n244: ### Signal 1: Rolling Average (weight 0.30)\n245: \n246: Averages the last 2 severity-weighted `newFindingsRatio` values from evidence-bearing iterations (excludes `thought` status). Votes STOP when the average drops below `rollingStopThreshold` (0.08).\n247: \n248: ```\n249: if len(evidenceIterations) >= 2:\n250:   recent = evidenceIterations[-2:]\n251:   avgRatio = mean(i.newFindingsRatio for i in recent)\n252:   rollingStop = avgRatio < 0.08\n253: ```\n254: \n255: ### Signal 2: MAD Noise Floor (weight 0.25)\n256: \n257: Robust statistical test using Median Absolute Deviation. Votes STOP when the latest ratio is at or below the computed noise floor.\n258: \n259: ```\n260: if len(evidenceIterations) >= 3:\n261:   allRatios = [i.newFindingsRatio for i in evidenceIterations]\n262:   med = median(allRatios)\n263:   mad = median([abs(r - med) for r in allRatios])\n264:   noiseFloor = mad * 1.4826     // normal distribution estimator\n265:   madStop = evidenceIterations[-1].newFindingsRatio <= noiseFloor\n266: ```\n267: \n268: ### Signal 3: Dimension Coverage (weight 0.45)\n269: \n270: Highest-weight signal. Votes STOP once every configured review dimension AND every required traceability protocol has been covered by at least one iteration, and the coverage set has been stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations (default 1). This is the signal the YAML workflow evaluates.\n271: \n272: ```\n273: dimensionStop =\n274:   dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count\n275:   AND required_traceability_protocols_covered\n276:   AND coverage_age >= config.minStabilizationPasses\n277: ```\n278: \n279: The latest severity-weighted newFindingsRatio is still tracked (the dashboard and registry surface it as `newFindingsRatio`), but it does NOT cast an independent stop vote, it feeds the rolling average and MAD noise-floor signals only.\n280: \n281: ### Weighted Vote\n282: \n283: ```\n284: stopScore = sum(s.weight * (1 if s.stop else 0) for s in signals) / totalWeight\n285: if stopScore >= 0.60:   // proceed to quality gate evaluation\n286: ```\n287: \n288: Weights are redistributed across active signals only. If only 2 signals have enough data, their weights are normalized to sum to 1.0.\n289: \n290: ### Semantic Convergence Signals\n291: \n292: Two additional signals provide deeper semantic analysis of review iteration quality. These signals are ADDITIONAL to the 3-signal composite vote above and participate in the legal-stop gate evaluation rather than the composite stop-score.\n293: \n294: #### semanticNovelty (0.0-1.0)\n295: \n296: Measures how much genuinely new review insight each iteration contributes beyond surface-level overlap with prior findings. Unlike `newFindingsRatio` (which is severity-weighted), `semanticNovelty` evaluates the conceptual novelty of findings independent of severity weighting.\n297: \n298: | Value | Meaning |\n299: |-------|---------|\n300: | 0.8-1.0 | Iteration uncovered substantially new defect patterns, architectural concerns, or review angles |\n301: | 0.4-0.7 | Mix of new review insights and restatements of prior findings |\n302: | 0.1-0.3 | Mostly refinements or rewordings of previously identified issues |\n303: | 0.0 | No semantically novel findings detected |\n304: \n305: Computation:\n306: ```\n307: function computeSemanticNovelty_review(currentFindings, priorCumulativeFindings):\n308:   newPatterns = extractDefectPatterns(currentFindings) - extractDefectPatterns(priorCumulativeFindings)\n309:   totalPatterns = extractDefectPatterns(currentFindings)\n310:   if len(totalPatterns) == 0: return 0.0\n311:   return len(newPatterns) / len(totalPatterns)\n312: ```\n313: \n314: When `semanticNovelty` drops below 0.15 for 2+ consecutive evidence iterations, it provides strong supporting evidence for a legal STOP decision. This signal catches cases where `newFindingsRatio` stays moderate (due to severity weighting of refinements) but the review has exhausted genuinely new defect categories.\n315: \n316: #### findingStability (0.0-1.0)\n317: \n318: Measures how stable the cumulative finding set is across iterations. A high stability score means the finding registry is not materially changing between iterations -- findings are not being added, upgraded, downgraded, or invalidated at a significant rate.\n319: \n320: | Value | Meaning |\n321: |-------|---------|\n322: | 0.9-1.0 | Finding set is highly stable, minimal churn between iterations |\n323: | 0.6-0.8 | Moderate stability, some findings still evolving |\n324: | 0.3-0.5 | Active churn, findings being added, merged, or reclassified frequently |\n325: | 0.0-0.2 | Highly unstable, the review is still in early discovery |\n326: \n327: Computation:\n328: ```\n329: function computeFindingStability(currentRegistry, priorRegistry):\n330:   if priorRegistry is null: return 0.0  // first iteration\n331:   unchangedFindings = count(f for f in currentRegistry\n332:     if f.id in priorRegistry and f.severity == priorRegistry[f.id].severity\n333:     and f.status == priorRegistry[f.id].status)\n334:   totalFindings = max(len(currentRegistry), len(priorRegistry))\n335:   if totalFindings == 0: return 1.0\n336:   return unchangedFindings / totalFindings\n337: ```\n338: \n339: Convergence behavior:\n340: - `findingStability >= 0.85` supports STOP: the finding set has stabilized and further iterations are unlikely to materially change the review outcome.\n341: - `findingStability < 0.50` prevents STOP: the finding set is still in flux and the review has not reached a stable assessment.\n342: \n343: #### Integration with Legal-Stop Gate Bundle\n344: \n345: The two semantic signals integrate with the existing 5-gate legal-stop bundle (Section 6):\n346: \n347: 1. **findingStability gate** (existing): The existing `findingStability` gate already evaluates rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio. The new `semanticNovelty` signal adds a sub-check:\n348:    - `semanticNoveltyPlateau`: `semanticNovelty < 0.15` for 2+ consecutive evidence iterations\n349:    - When this sub-check fails while the existing churn signals pass, the gate records the mismatch as a diagnostic note but does not independently block STOP.\n350: \n351: 2. **findingStability signal** (new): The `findingStability` metric (0.0-1.0) is surfaced alongside the existing convergence signals. It supports the `findingStability` gate evaluation by providing a registry-level stability measure that complements the ratio-based churn signals.\n352: \n353: The gate passes only when both the existing churn-based checks AND the semantic stability checks agree. When a semantic check fails, the persisted `blocked_stop.gateResults.findingStability` payload includes the semantic signal values.\n354: \n355: #### Stop-Decision Trace\n356: \n357: The stop-decision event includes which semantic signals supported or prevented STOP:\n358: \n359: ```json\n360: {\n361:   \"type\": \"event\",\n362:   \"event\": \"stop_decision\",\n363:   \"semanticSignals\": {\n364:     \"semanticNovelty\": { \"value\": 0.06, \"consecutiveLow\": 3, \"supportsStop\": true },\n365:     \"findingStability\": { \"value\": 0.92, \"supportsStop\": true }\n366:   },\n367:   \"semanticVerdict\": \"all_support_stop\",\n368:   ...\n369: }\n370: ```\n371: \n372: | `semanticVerdict` | Meaning |\n373: |-------------------|---------|\n374: | `all_support_stop` | Both semantic signals support stopping |\n375: | `mixed` | One signal supports stop, the other does not |\n376: | `all_prevent_stop` | Both semantic signals indicate more work is needed |\n377: | `insufficient_data` | Not enough iterations to compute semantic signals |\n378: \n379: ### Graceful Degradation\n380: \n381: | Iterations Completed | Active Signals | Behavior |\n382: |---------------------|----------------|----------|\n383: | 1 | Novelty ratio only (weight 1.0) | Very unlikely to stop without later confirmation from rolling churn signals |\n384: | 2 | Rolling avg + novelty ratio | Two-signal vote, reweighted |\n385: | 3+ | All three signals | Full composite, most reliable |\n386: \n387: Semantic convergence signals (`semanticNovelty`, `findingStability`) require at least 2 evidence iterations to produce meaningful values. They are omitted from legal-stop evaluation when insufficient data exists.\n388: \n389: ---\n390: \n391: ## 5. SEVERITY-WEIGHTED RATIO\n392: \n393: The review loop uses `newFindingsRatio` instead of `newInfoRatio`. It weights findings by severity so that critical discoveries count far more than minor suggestions.\n394: \n395: ### Severity Weights\n396: \n397: | Severity | Weight | Description |\n398: |----------|--------|-------------|\n399: | **P0** (Blocker) | 10.0 | Correctness failures, security vulnerabilities, spec contradictions |\n400: | **P1** (Required) | 5.0 | Degraded behavior, incomplete implementation, missing validation |\n401: | **P2** (Suggestion) | 1.0 | Style, naming, minor improvements, documentation gaps |\n402: \n403: ### Computation\n404: \n405: ```\n406: SEVERITY_WEIGHTS = { P0: 10.0, P1: 5.0, P2: 1.0 }\n407: refinementMultiplier = 0.5\n408: \n409: weightedNew       = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] for f in fully_new_findings)\n410: weightedRefinement = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] * 0.5 for f in refinement_findings)\n411: weightedTotal     = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] for f in all_findings_this_iteration)\n412: \n413: newFindingsRatio = (weightedNew + weightedRefinement) / weightedTotal\n414: ```\n415: \n416: - `fully_new_findings` -- findings not present in any prior iteration (new findingId).\n417: - `refinement_findings` -- findings that refine or upgrade an existing finding (same root cause, new evidence or severity change).\n418: - `refinementMultiplier = 0.5` -- refinements count at half weight.\n419: \n420: ### P0 Override Rule\n421: \n422: ```\n423: if ANY new P0 found this iteration:\n424:   newFindingsRatio = max(calculated, 0.50)\n425: \n426: if total_findings == 0:\n427:   newFindingsRatio = 0.0\n428: ```\n429: \n430: A new critical finding always signals significant remaining work. The 0.50 floor prevents premature convergence when critical issues are still being discovered.\n431: \n432: ---\n433: \n434: ## 6. LEGAL-STOP GATE BUNDLE\n435: \n436: > **GATE MODEL, two naming conventions mapped to one authoritative set.** The authoritative producer is `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`, which emits **9 gates** with the `Gate` suffix: `convergenceGate` / `dimensionCoverageGate` / `p0ResolutionGate` / `evidenceDensityGate` / `hotspotSaturationGate` / `claimAdjudicationGate` / `fixCompletenessReplayGate` / `candidateCoverageGate` / `graphlessFallbackGate`. The §Section-1 event shape (lines 98-119) mirrors this set verbatim and the reducer reads those names verbatim, so treat the event shape as authoritative when writing or reading JSONL state. The §6 table below is the high-level conceptual model and uses descriptive names WITHOUT the `Gate` suffix where one reads more naturally (for example `findingStability` maps to `convergenceGate`); each row carries its event-shape name so the mapping is explicit. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. The gate-model drift cluster (LG-0013, LG-0016, LG-0031, LG-0032) was reconciled in `006-gate-model-reconciliation`.\n437: \n438: Deep review treats STOP as legal only when the full review-specific gate bundle passes together. Convergence math may request STOP, but the workflow must still evaluate these 9 gates and persist a blocked-stop event when any gate fails.\n439: \n440: | Gate (§6 conceptual) | Event-shape name (§Section-1) | Rule | Fail Action |\n441: |------|------|------|-------------|\n442: | **findingStability** | `convergenceGate` | Rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio must all indicate low-yield review churn | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n443: | **dimensionCoverage** | `dimensionCoverageGate` | Every configured review dimension must have been examined at least once, with required traceability coverage stabilized | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n444: | **p0Resolution** | `p0ResolutionGate` | No unresolved P0 findings may remain active at stop time | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n445: | **evidenceDensity** | `evidenceDensityGate` | Evidence density across active findings must meet the configured threshold | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n446: | **hotspotSaturation** | `hotspotSaturationGate` | Review hotspots must be revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n447: | (no §6 counterpart) | `claimAdjudicationGate` | Each new P0/P1 finding must carry a typed adjudication packet, missing or failing packets veto STOP | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n448: | **fixCompletenessReplay** | `fixCompletenessReplayGate` | Security-sensitive fix reruns must replay previously closed P0/P1 gates and validate producer/consumer/matrix coverage from the remediation packet | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n449: | **candidateCoverage** (v2 rollout) | `candidateCoverageGate` | Search debt must be cleared and every required bug class must have candidate coverage before STOP, passes trivially when the v2 search path is inactive | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n450: | **graphlessFallback** (v2 rollout) | `graphlessFallbackGate` | When the code graph is unavailable, required bug classes must carry cited fallback ledger rows, passes trivially when the graph is available | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n451: \n452: ### Gate Evaluation\n453: \n454: ```\n455: function buildReviewLegalStop(state, config, coverage):\n456:   gateResults = {\n457:     findingStability: {\n458:       pass: rollingStop and madStop and state.latestNoveltyRatio <= config.convergenceThreshold,\n459:       detail: \"Rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio are all below stop thresholds.\"\n460:     },\n461:     dimensionCoverage: {\n462:       pass: everyConfiguredDimensionExaminedAtLeastOnce(coverage, config.reviewDimensions) and\n463:             coverage.requiredProtocolsCovered and\n464:             coverage.stabilizationPasses >= 1,\n465:       detail: \"All configured review dimensions have been examined, required traceability protocols are covered, and stabilization has aged enough to stop.\"\n466:     },\n467:     p0Resolution: {\n468:       pass: countActiveFindings(state, [\"P0\"]) == 0 and state.claimAdjudicationPassed != false,\n469:       detail: \"No unresolved P0 findings remain and blocker adjudication is complete.\"\n470:     },\n471:     evidenceDensity: {\n472:       pass: computeEvidenceDensity(state.activeFindings) >= config.evidenceDensityThreshold,\n473:       detail: \"Evidence density meets the configured threshold for active findings.\"\n474:     },\n475:     hotspotSaturation: {\n476:       pass: computeHotspotSaturation(state.hotspots) >= config.hotspotSaturationThreshold,\n477:       detail: \"Priority hotspots received enough revisits to satisfy saturation.\"\n478:     },\n479:     fixCompletenessReplay: {\n480:       pass: not isSecuritySensitiveFixRerun(state, config) or allRequiredReplayRowsPass(state.reviewReport),\n481:       detail: \"Security-sensitive fix reruns include closed-gate replay evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage before STOP.\"\n482:     },\n483:     candidateCoverage: {\n484:       pass: not isReviewDepthV2Active(state, config) or (searchDebtCleared(state) and allRequiredBugClassesCovered(state)),\n485:       detail: \"Search debt is cleared and every required bug class has candidate coverage. Passes trivially when the v2 search path is inactive.\"\n486:     },\n487:     graphlessFallback: {\n488:       pass: state.searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode == \"graph_available\" or allRequiredBugClassesHaveFallbackRows(state),\n489:       detail: \"When the code graph is unavailable, required bug classes carry cited fallback ledger rows. Passes trivially when the graph is available.\"\n490:     }\n491:   }\n492: \n493:   blockedBy = [name for name, result in gateResults.items() if not result.pass]\n494:   return {\n495:     pass: len(blockedBy) == 0,\n496:     blockedBy,\n497:     gateResults\n498:   }\n499: ```\n500: \n501: When convergence math returns STOP, invoke `buildReviewLegalStop()`. If it returns `pass: false`, persist a first-class `blocked_stop` event with the failing `blockedBy` gates, the full `gateResults` bundle, a `recoveryStrategy`, and the normal run/timestamp/session lineage fields before overriding the decision to CONTINUE.\n502: \n503: ### Blocked-Stop Recovery Strategy\n504: \n505: | Failed Gate | Recovery Strategy |\n506: |-------------|-------------------|\n507: | `findingStability` | Revisit the noisiest recent dimension and reduce novelty by closing obvious follow-up loops before re-checking STOP. |\n508: | `dimensionCoverage` | Schedule the next uncovered review dimension immediately. |\n509: | `p0Resolution` | Re-open the active blocker path and verify whether the P0 is real, downgraded, or still unresolved. |\n510: | `evidenceDensity` | Re-read weakly supported findings and add concrete `file:line` citations before they count toward a stop decision. |\n511: | `hotspotSaturation` | Revisit undersampled hotspots or adjacent call sites until the saturation heuristic passes. |\n512: | `fixCompletenessReplay` | Replay prior active or remediated P0/P1 gates, then record producer, consumer, and matrix coverage evidence before re-checking STOP. |\n513: | `candidateCoverage` | Clear outstanding search debt and run candidate discovery for the missing bug classes before re-checking STOP. |\n514: | `graphlessFallback` | Add cited fallback ledger rows for the required bug classes, or restore graph availability, before re-checking STOP. |\n515: \n516: ### Legacy Stop-Reason Mapping\n517: \n518: Use this table when replaying old packets or translating older prose/docs into the shared stop contract.\n519: \n520: | Legacy label | New `stopReason` | Mapping note |\n521: |--------------|------------------|--------------|\n522: | `all_dimensions_clean` | `converged` | Legacy review-specific terminal label, now expressed by the shared enum. |\n523: | `composite_converged` | `converged` | Legacy convergence-math wording now rolls into shared terminal success. |\n524: | `all dimensions clean` | `converged` | Old operator-facing prose for the same successful stop. |\n525: | `max_iterations_reached` | `maxIterationsReached` | Legacy machine label for the hard iteration cap. |\n526: | `max iterations` | `maxIterationsReached` | Old operator-facing hard-stop wording. |\n527: | `pause sentinel detected` | `userPaused` | Sentinel pause is now a shared user-directed stop reason. |\n528: | `guard_override` | `blockedStop` | Legacy continue override when a stop vote failed legal gates. |\n529: | `quality guard failed` | `blockedStop` | Older prose for the same blocked-stop outcome. |\n530: | `P0 override blocks convergence` | `blockedStop` | Legacy review wording for a stop attempt that was not legal to finalize. |\n531: | `stuck_detected` | `stuckRecovery` | Legacy recovery trigger label. |\n532: | `stuck_unrecoverable` | `stuckRecovery` | Legacy terminal wording for the same recovery path family. |\n533: | `manual halt` | `manualStop` | Operator-directed halt outside normal pause sentinel flow. |\n534: \n535: ---\n536: \n537: ## 7. PROVISIONAL VERDICT\n538: \n539: The provisional verdict is determined from active findings at the time the loop stops. It appears in both the convergence report and the final `review-report.md`.\n540: \n541: | Verdict | Condition | Meaning |\n542: |---------|-----------|---------|\n543: | **FAIL** | `activeP0 > 0` OR any legal-stop gate fails at terminal stop time | Does not meet quality standards. Blocks release. |\n544: | **CONDITIONAL** | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 > 0` | Meets threshold but has required fixes before release. |\n545: | **PASS** | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` | Shippable. Set `hasAdvisories: true` when `activeP2 > 0`. |\n546: \n547: ### Determination\n548: \n549: ```\n550: function determineVerdict(state, gateResult):\n551:   activeP0 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P0\"])\n552:   activeP1 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P1\"])\n553:   activeP2 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P2\"])\n554: \n555:   if activeP0 > 0 or not gateResult.passed:\n556:     return { verdict: \"FAIL\", nextCommand: \"/speckit:plan\" }\n557:   if activeP1 > 0:\n558:     return { verdict: \"CONDITIONAL\", nextCommand: \"/speckit:plan\" }\n559: \n560:   hasAdvisories = activeP2 > 0\n561:   return { verdict: \"PASS\", hasAdvisories, nextCommand: \"/create:changelog\" }\n562: ```\n563: \n564: ### Post-Verdict Routing\n565: \n566: | Verdict | Next Step |\n567: |---------|-----------|\n568: | FAIL | `/speckit:plan` -- create remediation plan from findings |\n569: | CONDITIONAL | `/speckit:plan` -- create fix plan for P1 findings |\n570: | PASS | `/create:changelog` -- record the clean audit |\n571: \n572: ---\n573: \n574: ## 8. RECOVERY, REPORTING, AND GRAPH-AWARE CONVERGENCE\n575: \n576: Stuck-recovery strategies, the convergence report format, and graph-aware review convergence live in `convergence-recovery.md` for navigability.\n577: \n578: ---\n579: \n580: ## OPTIMIZER-TUNABLE THRESHOLDS\n581: \n582: The following convergence thresholds are managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). Changes to these fields are proposed through the optimizer's advisory-only promotion gate and reviewed by humans before adoption.\n583: \n584: ### Tunable Fields (Optimizer-Managed)\n585: \n586: | Field | Default | Range | Description |\n587: |-------|---------|-------|-------------|\n588: | `convergenceThreshold` | 0.10 | 0.01-0.20 | General convergence sensitivity |\n589: | `stuckThreshold` | 2 | 1-5 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n590: | `maxIterations` | 7 | 3-20 | Hard iteration ceiling |\n591: | `compositeStopScore` | 0.60 | 0.40-0.80 | Weighted stop score needed before guard evaluation |\n592: \n593: ### Locked Fields (Not Optimizer-Tunable)\n594: \n595: The following fields are runtime contracts and MUST NOT be modified by the optimizer:\n596: \n597: - `stopReason` enum values and semantics\n598: - `blocked_stop` event structure and gate names\n599: - Lineage fields (`sessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`)\n600: - Reducer configuration and file protection policies\n601: - Review dimensions (`reviewDimensions`) and product mode (`mode`)\n602: \n603: ### Canonical Manifest\n604: \n605: The authoritative registry of tunable vs locked fields is maintained at:\n606: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json`\n\n(End of file - total 606 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Convergence\ndescription: Stop condition algorithms, quality guards, and recovery strategies for the autonomous deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review convergence detection\"\n  - \"severity weighted stop ratio\"\n  - \"legal stop gate bundle\"\n  - \"review stuck detection\"\n  - \"composite convergence vote\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.22\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence\n\nStop condition algorithms, quality guards, and stuck recovery for the deep review loop.\n\n---\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Convergence\ndescription: Stop condition algorithms, quality guards, and recovery strategies for the autonomous deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review convergence detection\"\n  - \"severity weighted stop ratio\"\n  - \"legal stop gate bundle\"\n  - \"review stuck detection\"\n  - \"composite convergence vote\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.22\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence\n\nStop condition algorithms, quality guards, and stuck recovery for the deep review loop.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nConvergence detection determines when the autonomous review loop should stop iterating. After every iteration the orchestrator evaluates three possible outcomes:\n\n| Outcome | Meaning |\n|---------|---------|\n| **CONTINUE** | More review work is expected to yield meaningful new findings. Dispatch the next iteration. |\n| **STOP** | The review has reached saturation. Proceed to synthesis and verdict. |\n| **STUCK_RECOVERY** | No progress detected for consecutive iterations. Attempt a recovery strategy before deciding. |\n\nConvergence is checked **after** each iteration completes and **before** the next iteration is dispatched. The check consumes the full JSONL state history and the current dimension coverage snapshot.\n\nRelease-readiness states are derived alongside convergence:\n- `in-progress` while coverage is incomplete or new P0/P1 findings are still appearing\n- `converged` once coverage and stabilization pass without new P0/P1 findings\n- `release-blocking` whenever unresolved P0 findings remain active\n\nWhen the loop stops and enters synthesis, the workflow emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md` from converged review deltas before compiling `review-report.md`. Operators can disable that write with `--no-resource-map`.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Evaluating whether the autonomous review loop should stop, continue, or recover.\n- Tuning convergence thresholds, stuck-recovery cadence, or stabilization windows.\n- Debugging a stuck-recovery escalation or a premature STOP vote.\n- Auditing the release-readiness classification logic before shipping.\n\n### Key Defaults\n\n| Setting | Value | Purpose |\n|---------|-------|---------|\n| `maxIterations` | 7 | Hard ceiling on loop iterations |\n| `convergenceThreshold` | 0.10 | General convergence sensitivity |\n| `rollingStopThreshold` | 0.08 | Rolling-average STOP vote threshold |\n| `noProgressThreshold` | 0.05 | Stuck / no-progress classification threshold |\n| `stuckThreshold` | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n| `minStabilizationPasses` | 1 | Coverage signal requires at least one stabilization pass |\n| `compositeStopScore` | 0.60 | Weighted stop-score needed before guard evaluation |\n\n### Threshold Semantics and Sibling Parity\n\n`convergenceThreshold` (default 0.10) compares new severity-weighted findings (P0=10, P1=5, P2=1) against accumulated findings. Lower values demand more iterations and a higher signal threshold before STOP is legal.\n\n**Not interchangeable with sibling deep-loop skills:**\n\n| Skill | Default | Signal |\n|---|---|---|\n| `deep-review` | 0.10 | severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 ratio |\n| `deep-research` | 0.05 | newInfoRatio (negative-knowledge emphasis) |\n| `deep-ai-council` (proposed) | 0.20 | adjudicator-verdict stability |\n\nCarrying threshold expectations across siblings will cause unexpected iteration counts. Tune each skill against its own default and its own signal, not by analogy.\n\n### Security-Sensitive Fix Overrides\n\n> **STATUS: SPEC ONLY (future implementation).** The override matrix below describes the contract that a future release should apply automatically when the review target involves security-sensitive surfaces. As of v1.9.0.0, the runtime does NOT auto-detect security-sensitivity and does NOT apply these overrides. `requiredClosedFindingReplay` and `requiredFixCompletenessGate` exist in no config / yaml / reducer surface (verified by grep). Operators running a security-sensitive review must manually tighten thresholds via `--convergence` + `--max-iterations` and manually maintain the closed-gate replay table. The contract below stands as the target spec for the next implementation pass. (Provenance for this deferred contract is recorded in this skill's changelog.)\n\nFor review reruns after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads (intended contract, not yet runtime-enforced):\n\n| Setting | General Default | Security-Sensitive Fix Default |\n|---------|-----------------|--------------------------------|\n| `minStabilizationPasses` | 1 | 2 |\n| `requiredClosedFindingReplay` | false | true for prior P0/P1 and any prior security/path P2 |\n| `requiredFixCompletenessGate` | false | true |\n\nWhen implemented, STOP must not be legal until the review report contains a closed-gate replay table that marks each prior active or remediated P0/P1 as `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `carried forward`, with file:line or command evidence. Operators today must enforce this rule manually.\n\n### Shared Stop Contract\n\nEvery terminal stop and every blocked-stop vote MUST emit the shared stop contract from REQ-001: a named `stopReason` enum plus, when STOP is vetoed, a `blocked_stop` event written to `deep-review-state.jsonl`. There is no nested `legalStop` wrapper on the persisted path. Earlier drafts of this document implied one, and that drift was the source of F009 in the 042 closing audit.\n\n### Convergence Modes\n\nThe shared convergence runtime accepts four values. Review legality, security gates, target authority, and verdict derivation remain owned by the review workflow rather than the convergence mode.\n\n| Mode | Live Behavior |\n|------|---------------|\n| `default` | Uses normal full-history convergence signals and sends a legal STOP to synthesis and verdict derivation. This is the fallback when no mode is supplied. |\n| `off` | Is accepted and persisted, but the shipped review YAML has no `off` decision branch; review therefore follows the same legal-stop and synthesis path as `default`. Use `stopPolicy: \"max-iterations\"` when convergence must remain telemetry-only until the iteration ceiling. |\n| `sliding-window` | Is accepted and persisted, but windowed graph-novelty telemetry is research-only in the shared runtime; review therefore retains its ordinary full-history signals, legal-stop gates, and synthesis path. |\n| `divergent` | After all review gates pass, translates the eligible `all_dimensions_clean` STOP into a read-only three-seat direction-selection pivot and continues with the selected review direction. |\n\n#### Divergent Pivot Contract\n\nReview has one eligible reason: the exact internal reason `all_dimensions_clean` with decision `STOP`. The nine legal-stop gates run before the divergent branch and remain unchanged. `maxIterationsReached`, `blockedStop`, `stuckRecovery`, `error`, `manualStop`, and `userPaused` are explicitly excluded. Max iterations, pause or cancellation, manual stop, unrecoverable error, and any blocked security or quality gate therefore never dispatch a pivot Council.\n\nEach eligible pivot runs one native, in-process Council round with exactly three distinct seats: analytical, critical, and pragmatic. It does not use an external CLI. The transaction requires all three seat returns to be parse-valid and at least two seats to materially endorse the same candidate without a high-severity blocker. Candidate sources are persisted unswept dimensions, search debt, producer-consumer gaps, negative-test gaps, and traceability gaps. Candidate generation rejects directions without in-scope evidence and directions that imply implementation, a fix, mutation, writing, or target expansion.\n\nThe guarantees are absolute: divergent mode never changes the PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL mapping, never authorizes a fix, and never makes the review target writable. A successful pivot returns to the loop before `phase_synthesis`; verdict computation exists only inside `phase_synthesis`, where active P0 yields FAIL, active P1 yields CONDITIONAL, and no active P0/P1 yields PASS. A failed pivot fails closed to that existing synthesis path.\n\nEvery pivot dispatches three seats, so a run that pivots has proportionally higher model cost and duration than the same run under `default`, `off`, or `sliding-window`. Pivot evidence is isolated under `<artifactRoot>/divergent/pivots/<pivotId>/council/**`, including config, append-only state, three seat artifacts, deliberation, and report. This path is distinct from ordinary planning Council artifacts under a spec packet's `ai-council/**` tree.\n\n#### stopReason Enum\n\n| `stopReason` | Meaning |\n|--------------|---------|\n| `converged` | All convergence signals met and legal-stop gates passed. |\n| `maxIterationsReached` | Iteration limit hit before convergence. |\n| `userPaused` | User requested pause via sentinel. |\n| `blockedStop` | Convergence math voted stop but legal-stop gates failed. |\n| `stuckRecovery` | Stuck detection triggered recovery. |\n| `error` | Unrecoverable error during iteration or reducer flow. |\n| `manualStop` | Operator explicitly halted outside the pause sentinel path. |\n\n#### blocked_stop Event (canonical, persisted)\n\n`step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` appends the following record to `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 5,\n  \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n  \"gateResults\": {\n    \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n    \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n      \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n    },\n    \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n    \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n    \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n    \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n    \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n    \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n    \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n  },\n  \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n  \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n- `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set emitted by `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n- `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n- `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.\n- When the graph convergence verdict is `STOP_BLOCKED`, fold the graph blocker gate name into `blockedBy` and preserve the structured blocker objects under `graphBlockerDetail`.\n\n### Decision Priority\n\nChecks are evaluated in this order (first match wins):\n\n1. **Max iterations** -- hard cap, always checked first.\n2. **All dimensions covered + clean** -- all 4 dimensions covered, no active P0/P1, stabilization passed, gates passed.\n3. **Stuck detection** -- 2+ consecutive no-progress iterations.\n4. **Composite convergence** -- 3-signal weighted vote with threshold 0.60.\n5. **Legal-stop gate bundle** -- review-specific stop gates. If a stop vote fails any gate, persist `stopReason=blockedStop` and continue.\n6. **Default CONTINUE** -- none of the above triggered.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HARD STOPS\n\nHard stops are evaluated first and override all other signals.\n\n### Max Iterations Reached\n\n```\nif len(iterations) >= config.maxIterations:       // default 7\n  return { action: \"STOP\", stopReason: \"maxIterationsReached\" }\n```\n\nThe loop stops unconditionally. Synthesis runs with whatever findings exist.\n\n### All Dimensions Covered with Stabilization\n\n```\nif coverage.dimensionCoverage == 1.0 and activeP0 == 0 and activeP1 == 0:\n  if stabilizationPasses >= config.coverageAge.minStabilizationPasses:\n    if buildReviewLegalStop(state, config, coverage).passed:\n      return { action: \"STOP\", stopReason: \"converged\" }\n```\n\nTriggers when all 4 dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability) are covered, no active P0/P1 remains, at least 1 stabilization pass has occurred, and the 5-gate legal-stop bundle passes. If gates fail, the loop records `stopReason=blockedStop` and continues despite full coverage.\n\n---\n\n## 3. STUCK DETECTION\n\nIdentifies when the review loop makes no meaningful progress across consecutive iterations.\n\n```\nfunction countConsecutiveStuck_review(evidenceIterations, noProgressThreshold):\n  count = 0\n  for i in reversed(evidenceIterations):\n    if i.status == \"thought\":   continue    // invisible to stuck counter\n    if i.status == \"insight\":   break       // resets stuck counter (genuine progress)\n    if i.newFindingsRatio < noProgressThreshold or i.status == \"stuck\":\n      count += 1\n    else:\n      break\n  return count\n```\n\n**Threshold:** `stuckThreshold = 2` consecutive no-progress iterations (using `noProgressThreshold = 0.05`).\n\n**Status exclusions:**\n- `insight`: Resets stuck counter -- a conceptual breakthrough counts as progress even with a low ratio.\n- `thought`: Skipped entirely -- analytical iterations produce no evidence to measure.\n\nWhen `stuckCount >= stuckThreshold`, the orchestrator invokes the recovery protocol (Section 8) before deciding whether to continue or stop.\n\nThe recovery entry uses `stopReason=stuckRecovery` while the loop is in recovery. If recovery later terminates the run, the terminal record keeps the same shared enum value instead of minting a review-only label.\n\n---\n\n## 4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE\n\nThree independent signals each cast a stop/continue vote. Stop when the weighted stop-score meets or exceeds the consensus threshold. The signal set below matches the authoritative 3-signal vote in `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml` `step_check_convergence` and the quick-reference convergence table, the 3rd signal is **dimension coverage**, not a standalone novelty ratio.\n\n| Signal | Weight | Min Iterations | Measures |\n|--------|--------|---------------|----------|\n| Rolling Average | 0.30 | 2 | Recent severity-weighted finding yield |\n| MAD Noise Floor | 0.25 | 3 | Signal vs noise in newFindingsRatio |\n| Dimension Coverage | 0.45 | 1 | Configured review dimensions fully covered AND required traceability protocols covered AND `coverage_age >= minStabilizationPasses` |\n\n### Signal 1: Rolling Average (weight 0.30)\n\nAverages the last 2 severity-weighted `newFindingsRatio` values from evidence-bearing iterations (excludes `thought` status). Votes STOP when the average drops below `rollingStopThreshold` (0.08).\n\n```\nif len(evidenceIterations) >= 2:\n  recent = evidenceIterations[-2:]\n  avgRatio = mean(i.newFindingsRatio for i in recent)\n  rollingStop = avgRatio < 0.08\n```\n\n### Signal 2: MAD Noise Floor (weight 0.25)\n\nRobust statistical test using Median Absolute Deviation. Votes STOP when the latest ratio is at or below the computed noise floor.\n\n```\nif len(evidenceIterations) >= 3:\n  allRatios = [i.newFindingsRatio for i in evidenceIterations]\n  med = median(allRatios)\n  mad = median([abs(r - med) for r in allRatios])\n  noiseFloor = mad * 1.4826     // normal distribution estimator\n  madStop = evidenceIterations[-1].newFindingsRatio <= noiseFloor\n```\n\n### Signal 3: Dimension Coverage (weight 0.45)\n\nHighest-weight signal. Votes STOP once every configured review dimension AND every required traceability protocol has been covered by at least one iteration, and the coverage set has been stable for at least `minStabilizationPasses` iterations (default 1). This is the signal the YAML workflow evaluates.\n\n```\ndimensionStop =\n  dimensions_covered_count == configured_dimensions_count\n  AND required_traceability_protocols_covered\n  AND coverage_age >= config.minStabilizationPasses\n```\n\nThe latest severity-weighted newFindingsRatio is still tracked (the dashboard and registry surface it as `newFindingsRatio`), but it does NOT cast an independent stop vote, it feeds the rolling average and MAD noise-floor signals only.\n\n### Weighted Vote\n\n```\nstopScore = sum(s.weight * (1 if s.stop else 0) for s in signals) / totalWeight\nif stopScore >= 0.60:   // proceed to quality gate evaluation\n```\n\nWeights are redistributed across active signals only. If only 2 signals have enough data, their weights are normalized to sum to 1.0.\n\n### Semantic Convergence Signals\n\nTwo additional signals provide deeper semantic analysis of review iteration quality. These signals are ADDITIONAL to the 3-signal composite vote above and participate in the legal-stop gate evaluation rather than the composite stop-score.\n\n#### semanticNovelty (0.0-1.0)\n\nMeasures how much genuinely new review insight each iteration contributes beyond surface-level overlap with prior findings. Unlike `newFindingsRatio` (which is severity-weighted), `semanticNovelty` evaluates the conceptual novelty of findings independent of severity weighting.\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.8-1.0 | Iteration uncovered substantially new defect patterns, architectural concerns, or review angles |\n| 0.4-0.7 | Mix of new review insights and restatements of prior findings |\n| 0.1-0.3 | Mostly refinements or rewordings of previously identified issues |\n| 0.0 | No semantically novel findings detected |\n\nComputation:\n```\nfunction computeSemanticNovelty_review(currentFindings, priorCumulativeFindings):\n  newPatterns = extractDefectPatterns(currentFindings) - extractDefectPatterns(priorCumulativeFindings)\n  totalPatterns = extractDefectPatterns(currentFindings)\n  if len(totalPatterns) == 0: return 0.0\n  return len(newPatterns) / len(totalPatterns)\n```\n\nWhen `semanticNovelty` drops below 0.15 for 2+ consecutive evidence iterations, it provides strong supporting evidence for a legal STOP decision. This signal catches cases where `newFindingsRatio` stays moderate (due to severity weighting of refinements) but the review has exhausted genuinely new defect categories.\n\n#### findingStability (0.0-1.0)\n\nMeasures how stable the cumulative finding set is across iterations. A high stability score means the finding registry is not materially changing between iterations -- findings are not being added, upgraded, downgraded, or invalidated at a significant rate.\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| 0.9-1.0 | Finding set is highly stable, minimal churn between iterations |\n| 0.6-0.8 | Moderate stability, some findings still evolving |\n| 0.3-0.5 | Active churn, findings being added, merged, or reclassified frequently |\n| 0.0-0.2 | Highly unstable, the review is still in early discovery |\n\nComputation:\n```\nfunction computeFindingStability(currentRegistry, priorRegistry):\n  if priorRegistry is null: return 0.0  // first iteration\n  unchangedFindings = count(f for f in currentRegistry\n    if f.id in priorRegistry and f.severity == priorRegistry[f.id].severity\n    and f.status == priorRegistry[f.id].status)\n  totalFindings = max(len(currentRegistry), len(priorRegistry))\n  if totalFindings == 0: return 1.0\n  return unchangedFindings / totalFindings\n```\n\nConvergence behavior:\n- `findingStability >= 0.85` supports STOP: the finding set has stabilized and further iterations are unlikely to materially change the review outcome.\n- `findingStability < 0.50` prevents STOP: the finding set is still in flux and the review has not reached a stable assessment.\n\n#### Integration with Legal-Stop Gate Bundle\n\nThe two semantic signals integrate with the existing 5-gate legal-stop bundle (Section 6):\n\n1. **findingStability gate** (existing): The existing `findingStability` gate already evaluates rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio. The new `semanticNovelty` signal adds a sub-check:\n   - `semanticNoveltyPlateau`: `semanticNovelty < 0.15` for 2+ consecutive evidence iterations\n   - When this sub-check fails while the existing churn signals pass, the gate records the mismatch as a diagnostic note but does not independently block STOP.\n\n2. **findingStability signal** (new): The `findingStability` metric (0.0-1.0) is surfaced alongside the existing convergence signals. It supports the `findingStability` gate evaluation by providing a registry-level stability measure that complements the ratio-based churn signals.\n\nThe gate passes only when both the existing churn-based checks AND the semantic stability checks agree. When a semantic check fails, the persisted `blocked_stop.gateResults.findingStability` payload includes the semantic signal values.\n\n#### Stop-Decision Trace\n\nThe stop-decision event includes which semantic signals supported or prevented STOP:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"stop_decision\",\n  \"semanticSignals\": {\n    \"semanticNovelty\": { \"value\": 0.06, \"consecutiveLow\": 3, \"supportsStop\": true },\n    \"findingStability\": { \"value\": 0.92, \"supportsStop\": true }\n  },\n  \"semanticVerdict\": \"all_support_stop\",\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n| `semanticVerdict` | Meaning |\n|-------------------|---------|\n| `all_support_stop` | Both semantic signals support stopping |\n| `mixed` | One signal supports stop, the other does not |\n| `all_prevent_stop` | Both semantic signals indicate more work is needed |\n| `insufficient_data` | Not enough iterations to compute semantic signals |\n\n### Graceful Degradation\n\n| Iterations Completed | Active Signals | Behavior |\n|---------------------|----------------|----------|\n| 1 | Novelty ratio only (weight 1.0) | Very unlikely to stop without later confirmation from rolling churn signals |\n| 2 | Rolling avg + novelty ratio | Two-signal vote, reweighted |\n| 3+ | All three signals | Full composite, most reliable |\n\nSemantic convergence signals (`semanticNovelty`, `findingStability`) require at least 2 evidence iterations to produce meaningful values. They are omitted from legal-stop evaluation when insufficient data exists.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SEVERITY-WEIGHTED RATIO\n\nThe review loop uses `newFindingsRatio` instead of `newInfoRatio`. It weights findings by severity so that critical discoveries count far more than minor suggestions.\n\n### Severity Weights\n\n| Severity | Weight | Description |\n|----------|--------|-------------|\n| **P0** (Blocker) | 10.0 | Correctness failures, security vulnerabilities, spec contradictions |\n| **P1** (Required) | 5.0 | Degraded behavior, incomplete implementation, missing validation |\n| **P2** (Suggestion) | 1.0 | Style, naming, minor improvements, documentation gaps |\n\n### Computation\n\n```\nSEVERITY_WEIGHTS = { P0: 10.0, P1: 5.0, P2: 1.0 }\nrefinementMultiplier = 0.5\n\nweightedNew       = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] for f in fully_new_findings)\nweightedRefinement = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] * 0.5 for f in refinement_findings)\nweightedTotal     = sum(SEVERITY_WEIGHTS[f.severity] for f in all_findings_this_iteration)\n\nnewFindingsRatio = (weightedNew + weightedRefinement) / weightedTotal\n```\n\n- `fully_new_findings` -- findings not present in any prior iteration (new findingId).\n- `refinement_findings` -- findings that refine or upgrade an existing finding (same root cause, new evidence or severity change).\n- `refinementMultiplier = 0.5` -- refinements count at half weight.\n\n### P0 Override Rule\n\n```\nif ANY new P0 found this iteration:\n  newFindingsRatio = max(calculated, 0.50)\n\nif total_findings == 0:\n  newFindingsRatio = 0.0\n```\n\nA new critical finding always signals significant remaining work. The 0.50 floor prevents premature convergence when critical issues are still being discovered.\n\n---\n\n## 6. LEGAL-STOP GATE BUNDLE\n\n> **GATE MODEL, two naming conventions mapped to one authoritative set.** The authoritative producer is `step_emit_blocked_stop` in both `deep_review_{auto,confirm}.yaml`, which emits **9 gates** with the `Gate` suffix: `convergenceGate` / `dimensionCoverageGate` / `p0ResolutionGate` / `evidenceDensityGate` / `hotspotSaturationGate` / `claimAdjudicationGate` / `fixCompletenessReplayGate` / `candidateCoverageGate` / `graphlessFallbackGate`. The §Section-1 event shape (lines 98-119) mirrors this set verbatim and the reducer reads those names verbatim, so treat the event shape as authoritative when writing or reading JSONL state. The §6 table below is the high-level conceptual model and uses descriptive names WITHOUT the `Gate` suffix where one reads more naturally (for example `findingStability` maps to `convergenceGate`); each row carries its event-shape name so the mapping is explicit. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates that pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive. The gate-model drift cluster (LG-0013, LG-0016, LG-0031, LG-0032) was reconciled in `006-gate-model-reconciliation`.\n\nDeep review treats STOP as legal only when the full review-specific gate bundle passes together. Convergence math may request STOP, but the workflow must still evaluate these 9 gates and persist a blocked-stop event when any gate fails.\n\n| Gate (§6 conceptual) | Event-shape name (§Section-1) | Rule | Fail Action |\n|------|------|------|-------------|\n| **findingStability** | `convergenceGate` | Rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio must all indicate low-yield review churn | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **dimensionCoverage** | `dimensionCoverageGate` | Every configured review dimension must have been examined at least once, with required traceability coverage stabilized | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **p0Resolution** | `p0ResolutionGate` | No unresolved P0 findings may remain active at stop time | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **evidenceDensity** | `evidenceDensityGate` | Evidence density across active findings must meet the configured threshold | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **hotspotSaturation** | `hotspotSaturationGate` | Review hotspots must be revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| (no §6 counterpart) | `claimAdjudicationGate` | Each new P0/P1 finding must carry a typed adjudication packet, missing or failing packets veto STOP | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **fixCompletenessReplay** | `fixCompletenessReplayGate` | Security-sensitive fix reruns must replay previously closed P0/P1 gates and validate producer/consumer/matrix coverage from the remediation packet | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **candidateCoverage** (v2 rollout) | `candidateCoverageGate` | Search debt must be cleared and every required bug class must have candidate coverage before STOP, passes trivially when the v2 search path is inactive | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n| **graphlessFallback** (v2 rollout) | `graphlessFallbackGate` | When the code graph is unavailable, required bug classes must carry cited fallback ledger rows, passes trivially when the graph is available | Block STOP, persist `blockedStop` |\n\n### Gate Evaluation\n\n```\nfunction buildReviewLegalStop(state, config, coverage):\n  gateResults = {\n    findingStability: {\n      pass: rollingStop and madStop and state.latestNoveltyRatio <= config.convergenceThreshold,\n      detail: \"Rolling average, MAD noise floor, and novelty ratio are all below stop thresholds.\"\n    },\n    dimensionCoverage: {\n      pass: everyConfiguredDimensionExaminedAtLeastOnce(coverage, config.reviewDimensions) and\n            coverage.requiredProtocolsCovered and\n            coverage.stabilizationPasses >= 1,\n      detail: \"All configured review dimensions have been examined, required traceability protocols are covered, and stabilization has aged enough to stop.\"\n    },\n    p0Resolution: {\n      pass: countActiveFindings(state, [\"P0\"]) == 0 and state.claimAdjudicationPassed != false,\n      detail: \"No unresolved P0 findings remain and blocker adjudication is complete.\"\n    },\n    evidenceDensity: {\n      pass: computeEvidenceDensity(state.activeFindings) >= config.evidenceDensityThreshold,\n      detail: \"Evidence density meets the configured threshold for active findings.\"\n    },\n    hotspotSaturation: {\n      pass: computeHotspotSaturation(state.hotspots) >= config.hotspotSaturationThreshold,\n      detail: \"Priority hotspots received enough revisits to satisfy saturation.\"\n    },\n    fixCompletenessReplay: {\n      pass: not isSecuritySensitiveFixRerun(state, config) or allRequiredReplayRowsPass(state.reviewReport),\n      detail: \"Security-sensitive fix reruns include closed-gate replay evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage before STOP.\"\n    },\n    candidateCoverage: {\n      pass: not isReviewDepthV2Active(state, config) or (searchDebtCleared(state) and allRequiredBugClassesCovered(state)),\n      detail: \"Search debt is cleared and every required bug class has candidate coverage. Passes trivially when the v2 search path is inactive.\"\n    },\n    graphlessFallback: {\n      pass: state.searchCoverage.graphCoverageMode == \"graph_available\" or allRequiredBugClassesHaveFallbackRows(state),\n      detail: \"When the code graph is unavailable, required bug classes carry cited fallback ledger rows. Passes trivially when the graph is available.\"\n    }\n  }\n\n  blockedBy = [name for name, result in gateResults.items() if not result.pass]\n  return {\n    pass: len(blockedBy) == 0,\n    blockedBy,\n    gateResults\n  }\n```\n\nWhen convergence math returns STOP, invoke `buildReviewLegalStop()`. If it returns `pass: false`, persist a first-class `blocked_stop` event with the failing `blockedBy` gates, the full `gateResults` bundle, a `recoveryStrategy`, and the normal run/timestamp/session lineage fields before overriding the decision to CONTINUE.\n\n### Blocked-Stop Recovery Strategy\n\n| Failed Gate | Recovery Strategy |\n|-------------|-------------------|\n| `findingStability` | Revisit the noisiest recent dimension and reduce novelty by closing obvious follow-up loops before re-checking STOP. |\n| `dimensionCoverage` | Schedule the next uncovered review dimension immediately. |\n| `p0Resolution` | Re-open the active blocker path and verify whether the P0 is real, downgraded, or still unresolved. |\n| `evidenceDensity` | Re-read weakly supported findings and add concrete `file:line` citations before they count toward a stop decision. |\n| `hotspotSaturation` | Revisit undersampled hotspots or adjacent call sites until the saturation heuristic passes. |\n| `fixCompletenessReplay` | Replay prior active or remediated P0/P1 gates, then record producer, consumer, and matrix coverage evidence before re-checking STOP. |\n| `candidateCoverage` | Clear outstanding search debt and run candidate discovery for the missing bug classes before re-checking STOP. |\n| `graphlessFallback` | Add cited fallback ledger rows for the required bug classes, or restore graph availability, before re-checking STOP. |\n\n### Legacy Stop-Reason Mapping\n\nUse this table when replaying old packets or translating older prose/docs into the shared stop contract.\n\n| Legacy label | New `stopReason` | Mapping note |\n|--------------|------------------|--------------|\n| `all_dimensions_clean` | `converged` | Legacy review-specific terminal label, now expressed by the shared enum. |\n| `composite_converged` | `converged` | Legacy convergence-math wording now rolls into shared terminal success. |\n| `all dimensions clean` | `converged` | Old operator-facing prose for the same successful stop. |\n| `max_iterations_reached` | `maxIterationsReached` | Legacy machine label for the hard iteration cap. |\n| `max iterations` | `maxIterationsReached` | Old operator-facing hard-stop wording. |\n| `pause sentinel detected` | `userPaused` | Sentinel pause is now a shared user-directed stop reason. |\n| `guard_override` | `blockedStop` | Legacy continue override when a stop vote failed legal gates. |\n| `quality guard failed` | `blockedStop` | Older prose for the same blocked-stop outcome. |\n| `P0 override blocks convergence` | `blockedStop` | Legacy review wording for a stop attempt that was not legal to finalize. |\n| `stuck_detected` | `stuckRecovery` | Legacy recovery trigger label. |\n| `stuck_unrecoverable` | `stuckRecovery` | Legacy terminal wording for the same recovery path family. |\n| `manual halt` | `manualStop` | Operator-directed halt outside normal pause sentinel flow. |\n\n---\n\n## 7. PROVISIONAL VERDICT\n\nThe provisional verdict is determined from active findings at the time the loop stops. It appears in both the convergence report and the final `review-report.md`.\n\n| Verdict | Condition | Meaning |\n|---------|-----------|---------|\n| **FAIL** | `activeP0 > 0` OR any legal-stop gate fails at terminal stop time | Does not meet quality standards. Blocks release. |\n| **CONDITIONAL** | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 > 0` | Meets threshold but has required fixes before release. |\n| **PASS** | `activeP0 == 0` AND `activeP1 == 0` | Shippable. Set `hasAdvisories: true` when `activeP2 > 0`. |\n\n### Determination\n\n```\nfunction determineVerdict(state, gateResult):\n  activeP0 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P0\"])\n  activeP1 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P1\"])\n  activeP2 = countActiveFindings(state, [\"P2\"])\n\n  if activeP0 > 0 or not gateResult.passed:\n    return { verdict: \"FAIL\", nextCommand: \"/speckit:plan\" }\n  if activeP1 > 0:\n    return { verdict: \"CONDITIONAL\", nextCommand: \"/speckit:plan\" }\n\n  hasAdvisories = activeP2 > 0\n  return { verdict: \"PASS\", hasAdvisories, nextCommand: \"/create:changelog\" }\n```\n\n### Post-Verdict Routing\n\n| Verdict | Next Step |\n|---------|-----------|\n| FAIL | `/speckit:plan` -- create remediation plan from findings |\n| CONDITIONAL | `/speckit:plan` -- create fix plan for P1 findings |\n| PASS | `/create:changelog` -- record the clean audit |\n\n---\n\n## 8. RECOVERY, REPORTING, AND GRAPH-AWARE CONVERGENCE\n\nStuck-recovery strategies, the convergence report format, and graph-aware review convergence live in `convergence-recovery.md` for navigability.\n\n---\n\n## OPTIMIZER-TUNABLE THRESHOLDS\n\nThe following convergence thresholds are managed by the offline loop optimizer (042.004). Changes to these fields are proposed through the optimizer's advisory-only promotion gate and reviewed by humans before adoption.\n\n### Tunable Fields (Optimizer-Managed)\n\n| Field | Default | Range | Description |\n|-------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `convergenceThreshold` | 0.10 | 0.01-0.20 | General convergence sensitivity |\n| `stuckThreshold` | 2 | 1-5 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n| `maxIterations` | 7 | 3-20 | Hard iteration ceiling |\n| `compositeStopScore` | 0.60 | 0.40-0.80 | Weighted stop score needed before guard evaluation |\n\n### Locked Fields (Not Optimizer-Tunable)\n\nThe following fields are runtime contracts and MUST NOT be modified by the optimizer:\n\n- `stopReason` enum values and semantics\n- `blocked_stop` event structure and gate names\n- Lineage fields (`sessionId`, `lineageMode`, `generation`)\n- Reducer configuration and file protection policies\n- Review dimensions (`reviewDimensions`) and product mode (`mode`)\n\n### Canonical Manifest\n\nThe authoritative registry of tunable vs locked fields is maintained at:\n`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/optimizer/optimizer-manifest.json`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":606,"totalLines":606,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","time":{"start":1786124673613,"end":1786124673623}},"id":"prt_fdd53a123001SFJ7lUP8F1LqDl","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd5380ae001jYZVupJikls230"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786124673915,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_VeBcLw3JDwLzD1DBl1vA7824","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\n3: description: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n6:   - \"review stop signals\"\n7:   - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n8:   - \"review blocked stop\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.3\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Convergence Signals\n15: \n16: This reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: Deep-review convergence is a release-readiness decision. The loop stops only when severity-weighted findings stabilize, dimension coverage is complete, quality gates pass, and no P0 override is active.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. SIGNALS\n27: \n28: | Signal | Meaning | Blocks STOP When |\n29: |--------|---------|------------------|\n30: | Severity-weighted new findings | Weighted P0/P1/P2 discovery ratio for the latest iteration | Above the configured threshold |\n31: | Rolling stop average | Stabilized trend across recent iterations | Still above the stop band |\n32: | Dimension coverage | Required review dimensions and traceability overlays covered | Any required dimension is missing |\n33: | Quality-gate bundle | Evidence, scope, coverage, P0, density, hotspot, claim, candidate, graphless gates | Any required gate fails |\n34: | Graph-aware blind spot check | Coverage graph sees unresolved structural gaps | Graph blockers remain active |\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. P0 OVERRIDE\n39: \n40: Any new P0 forces at least one more iteration. The override exists because a new blocker changes the release verdict, even if the rest of the stop math appears stable.\n41: \n42: P0 handling requires:\n43: \n44: - File and line evidence.\n45: - Adversarial self-check.\n46: - Active registry update.\n47: - Replay in synthesis before PASS is legal.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. LEGAL STOP\n52: \n53: STOP is legal only when all of these are true:\n54: \n55: 1. New findings are below threshold.\n56: 2. Rolling trend is stable.\n57: 3. All required dimensions are covered.\n58: 4. The quality-gate bundle passes.\n59: 5. No unresolved P0 remains.\n60: 6. Graph-aware blockers are absent or explicitly unavailable with fallback evidence.\n61: \n62: If any item fails, the workflow emits `blocked_stop` and continues or routes to recovery.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: ## 5. SIBLING CONTRAST\n67: \n68: Do not carry thresholds across deep skills:\n69: \n70: | Skill | Primary Signal | Default Threshold |\n71: |-------|----------------|-------------------|\n72: | `deep-review` | Severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 new findings | `0.10` |\n73: | `deep-research` | Novelty/newInfoRatio over research knowledge | `0.05` |\n74: | `deep-ai-council` | Planning agreement with critique blocker check | Council-specific, not interchangeable |\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n79: \n80: - `references/convergence/convergence.md` for the full stop contract.\n81: - `references/state/state-outputs.md` for dashboard and report fields that display convergence.\n82: - `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer-owned gate state.\n\n(End of file - total 82 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n  - \"review stop signals\"\n  - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n  - \"review blocked stop\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence Signals\n\nThis reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n  - \"review stop signals\"\n  - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n  - \"review blocked stop\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence Signals\n\nThis reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDeep-review convergence is a release-readiness decision. The loop stops only when severity-weighted findings stabilize, dimension coverage is complete, quality gates pass, and no P0 override is active.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SIGNALS\n\n| Signal | Meaning | Blocks STOP When |\n|--------|---------|------------------|\n| Severity-weighted new findings | Weighted P0/P1/P2 discovery ratio for the latest iteration | Above the configured threshold |\n| Rolling stop average | Stabilized trend across recent iterations | Still above the stop band |\n| Dimension coverage | Required review dimensions and traceability overlays covered | Any required dimension is missing |\n| Quality-gate bundle | Evidence, scope, coverage, P0, density, hotspot, claim, candidate, graphless gates | Any required gate fails |\n| Graph-aware blind spot check | Coverage graph sees unresolved structural gaps | Graph blockers remain active |\n\n---\n\n## 3. P0 OVERRIDE\n\nAny new P0 forces at least one more iteration. The override exists because a new blocker changes the release verdict, even if the rest of the stop math appears stable.\n\nP0 handling requires:\n\n- File and line evidence.\n- Adversarial self-check.\n- Active registry update.\n- Replay in synthesis before PASS is legal.\n\n---\n\n## 4. LEGAL STOP\n\nSTOP is legal only when all of these are true:\n\n1. New findings are below threshold.\n2. Rolling trend is stable.\n3. All required dimensions are covered.\n4. The quality-gate bundle passes.\n5. No unresolved P0 remains.\n6. Graph-aware blockers are absent or explicitly unavailable with fallback evidence.\n\nIf any item fails, the workflow emits `blocked_stop` and continues or routes to recovery.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SIBLING CONTRAST\n\nDo not carry thresholds across deep skills:\n\n| Skill | Primary Signal | Default Threshold |\n|-------|----------------|-------------------|\n| `deep-review` | Severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 new findings | `0.10` |\n| `deep-research` | Novelty/newInfoRatio over research knowledge | `0.05` |\n| `deep-ai-council` | Planning agreement with critique blocker check | Council-specific, not interchangeable |\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/convergence/convergence.md` for the full stop contract.\n- `references/state/state-outputs.md` for dashboard and report fields that display convergence.\n- `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer-owned gate state.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":82,"totalLines":82,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","time":{"start":1786124673910,"end":1786124673914}},"id":"prt_fdd53a27c001SspsDVxPsBO6Op","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd5380ae001jYZVupJikls230"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1786124673947,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"id":"prt_fdd539fe5001mS5nWWP51zHu6i","messageID":"msg_fdd5380ae001jYZVupJikls230","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","type":"text","text":"I have the full picture now. Let me read the convergence references and the auto workflow YAML to follow the exact loop contract.","time":{"start":1786124672997,"end":1786124673945}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786124675303,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"id":"prt_fdd53a8e40014kUwybNcpANMIW","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fdd5380ae001jYZVupJikls230","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":94350,"input":514,"output":179,"reasoning":601,"cache":{"write":0,"read":93056}},"cost":0.0005509168}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786124678942,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"id":"prt_fdd53b71b001I7c3ncuFgVwcz0","messageID":"msg_fdd53ae51001j39l3BT9X77daz","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786124680559,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_JnY7pmhW0f8pOQ5VX67e2517","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: # DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n5: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: role: Deep Review Loop Manager\n7: purpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\n8: action: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\n9: operating_mode:\n10:   workflow: iterative_loop\n11:   workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n12:   workflow_execution: autonomous\n13:   approvals: none\n14:   tracking: progressive_review_state\n15:   validation: convergence_detection\n16: \n17: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n18: # OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n19: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: operating_principles:\n21:   core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n22:   approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n23:   mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n24: \n25: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n26: # USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n27: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n28: user_inputs:\n29:   review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n30:   review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n31:   review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability] - Dimensions to check. Default: all.\"\n32:   spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n33:   session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n34:   lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime only persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive) and `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived). `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and no longer accepted — see deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n35:   max_iterations: 7\n36:   convergence_threshold: 0.10\n37:   convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n38:   stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n39:   config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n40: \n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: # CONTEXT LOADING\n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: context_loading:\n45:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n46:   purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n47:   mcp_integration:\n48:     tool: memory_context\n49:     note: \"Call MCP tools directly - NEVER through Code Mode\"\n50:     parameters: { input: \"{review_target}\", mode: \"focused\", intent: \"understand\", includeContent: true }\n51:   when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n52:   behavior:\n53:     if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n54:     if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n55: \n56: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n57: # SKILL REFERENCE\n58: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n59: skill_reference:\n60:   skill: system-deep-loop\n61:   skill_md: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n62:   references:\n63:     loop_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n64:     state_format: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n65:     convergence: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n66:   templates:\n67:     config: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n68:     strategy: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n69: \n70: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n71: # AGENT CONFIGURATION\n72: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n73: agent_config:\n74:   agent: deep-review\n75:   agent_file: \".opencode/agents/deep-review.md\"\n76:   # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n77:   mode: subagent\n78:   model: opus\n79:   leaf_only: true\n80:   tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n81:   mcp_servers: [mk-spec-memory]\n82:   tool_call_budget: { target: 9, soft_max: 12, hard_max: 13 }\n83: \n84: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n85: # STATE FILE PATHS\n86: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n87: state_paths:\n88:   # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n89:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n90:   # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n91:   # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n92:   # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n93:   packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n94:   local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n95:   legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n96:   config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n97:   state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n98:   findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n99:   strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n100:   dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n101:   pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n102:   lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n103:   prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n104:   iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n105:   iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n106:   # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n107:   # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n108:   # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n109:   delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n110:   delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n111:   review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n112:   resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n113:   archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n114: \n115: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n116: # WORKFLOW\n117: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n118: workflow:\n119: \n120:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n121:     description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n122:     note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n123:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n124:     if_present:\n125:       bind:\n126:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n127:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n128:         artifact_subfolder: null\n129:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n130:     if_absent:\n131:       command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n132:       outputs:\n133:         - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n134:         - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n135:         - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n136:         - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n137: \n138:   step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n139:     description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n140:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n141:     if_present:\n142:       bind:\n143:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n144:     if_absent:\n145:       bind:\n146:         reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n147: \n148:   step_apply_lifecycle_request:\n149:     description: \"Honor explicit auto-mode restart before fan-out or normal initialization\"\n150:     skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n151:     instructions: |\n152:       This is the autonomous equivalent of the confirm-mode restart choice. Run it\n153:       immediately after artifact resolution and before fan-out so old packet files\n154:       cannot be merged with fresh lineage outputs. A restart request must never\n155:       fall back to auto-resume. In auto mode, the explicit restart flag is operator\n156:       authorization to archive the resolved review packet, so do not ask for a\n157:       second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped archive back to\n158:       the packet directory.\n159:     command: \"if [ -d \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" ]; then mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}\\\" && mv \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\\\"; fi; mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\"\"\n160:     outputs:\n161:       - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n162:       - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n163:     on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n164: \n165:   step_fanout_spawn:\n166:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n167:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n168:     instructions: |\n169:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n170:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n171:       A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n172:       session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n173:       self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n174:       first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n175:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n176:       deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n177:       deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n178:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n179:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n180:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n181:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n182:     sub_steps:\n183:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n184:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n185:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n186:         command: |\n187:           node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n188:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n189:             --loop-type review \\\n190:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n191:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n192:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n193:             --stop-policy {stop_policy}\n194:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n195:         wait_for_completion: true\n196: \n197:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n198:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n199:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n200:   phase_init:\n201:     purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n202:     steps:\n203: \n204:       step_preflight_contract:\n205:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n206:         verify:\n207:           - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n208:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n209:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n210:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n211:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n212: \n213:       step_create_directories:\n214:         action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n215:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n216: \n217:       step_detect_resource_map:\n218:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n219:         inspect:\n220:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n221:         classify:\n222:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n223:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n224:         outputs:\n225:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n226:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n227: \n228:       step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n229:         action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n230:         detect:\n231:           canonical_review_state:\n232:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n233:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n234:             - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n235:             - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n236:           legacy_review_state:\n237:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n238:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n239:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n240:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n241:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n242:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n243:             - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n244:             - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n245:           legacy_review_markers:\n246:             - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n247:             - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n248:         migrate_only:\n249:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n250:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n251:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n252:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n253:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n254:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n255:           - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n256:           - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n257:         on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n258:         on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, append a migration event to the canonical JSONL, and leave unrelated scratch files untouched.\"\n259:         on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n260:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir} && if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}; find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; ; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}; [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}; if [ -e {state_paths.state_log} ]; then printf '%s\\n' '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"migration\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"review\\\",\\\"legacyArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-research-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-research-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-research-pause\\\"],\\\"canonicalArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-review-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-review-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-review-pause\\\"],\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\\\"}' >> {state_paths.state_log}; fi; fi; find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; 2>/dev/null || true\"\n261: \n262:       step_acquire_lock:\n263:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n264:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder}\"\n265:         on_acquire: \"Capture ownerPid from the JSON output and reuse it for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n266:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls; stale-lock override is confirm-only or explicit recovery-only.\"\n267:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n268:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n269:         on_halt:\n270:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n271:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\"]\n272:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n273:         on_cancel:\n274:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n275:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n276:         on_workflow_exit:\n277:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n278:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n279: \n280:       step_classify_session:\n281:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n282:         inspect:\n283:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n284:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n285:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n286:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n287:         classify:\n288:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n289:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n290:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n291:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n292:         outputs:\n293:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n294:         lifecycle_routing:\n295:           - \"If lineage_mode == restart and session_state is resume or completed-session, execute on_restart before on_resume or on_completed_session.\"\n296:           - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n297:         on_resume:\n298:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n299:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n300:           skip_to: phase_loop\n301:         on_restart:\n302:           action: \"Archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n303:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n304:           set:\n305:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n306:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n307:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n308:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n309:           skip_to: step_create_config\n310:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n311:         on_completed_session:\n312:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n313:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n314:         on_invalid_state:\n315:           halt: true\n316:           message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n317:         on_fresh:\n318:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n319: \n320:       step_scope_discovery:\n321:         action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n322:         resolve:\n323:           spec-folder: |\n324:             1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, checklist.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n325:             2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n326:             3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n327:             4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n328:             5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n329:             6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n330:           skill: |\n331:             1. Read SKILL.md from .opencode/skills/{skill_name}/\n332:             2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n333:             3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n334:             4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n335:             5. Set scope = all discovered files\n336:           agent: |\n337:             1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .opencode/agents/)\n338:             2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n339:             3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n340:           track: |\n341:             1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n342:             2. For each: read spec.md + checklist.md\n343:             3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n344:           files: |\n345:             1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n346:             2. Validate all files exist\n347:             3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n348:             4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n349:         outputs:\n350:           - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n351:           - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n352: \n353:       step_order_dimensions:\n354:         action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n355:         algorithm: |\n356:           1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n357:           2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n358:              correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n359:           3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions\n360:           4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n361:              - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n362:              - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n363:           5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n364:           6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n365:         outputs:\n366:           - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n367:           - inventory_pass: true\n368: \n369:       step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n370:         action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n371:         outputs:\n372:           - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n373:           - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n374:         normalize: |\n375:           Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n376:             - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n377:             - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n378:             - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n379:           Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.\n380: \n381:       step_resolve_session_id:\n382:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n383:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n384:         if_present:\n385:           bind:\n386:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n387:         if_absent:\n388:           bind:\n389:             session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n390: \n391:       step_create_config:\n392:         action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n393:         template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n394:         populate:\n395:           topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n396:           mode: \"review\"\n397:           sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n398:           parentSessionId: null\n399:           lineageMode: \"new\"\n400:           generation: 1\n401:           continuedFromRun: null\n402:           reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n403:           reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n404:           # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n405:           reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n406:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n407:           reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n408:           severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n409:           crossReference:\n410:             core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n411:             overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n412:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n413:           # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n414:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n415:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n416:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n417:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n418:           stuckThreshold: 2\n419:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n420:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n421:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n422:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n423:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n424:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n425:           status: \"initialized\"\n426:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n427:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n428:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n429: \n430:       step_create_state_log:\n431:         action: \"Initialize JSONL state log with config record including review fields and lineage metadata\"\n432:         note: \"Reuse review_dimensions_json from step_normalize_review_dimensions. Never re-normalize or wrap the raw template value.\"\n433:         # Same parsed --no-resource-map flag honored here so config and state_log agree from line 1.\n434:         content: '{\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"reviewTarget\":\"{review_target}\",\"reviewTargetType\":\"{review_target_type}\",\"reviewDimensions\":{review_dimensions_json},\"resource_map_present\":{resource_map_present},\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":{resource_map_emit}},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"convergenceThreshold\":{convergence_threshold},\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"{convergence_mode}\",\"divergent\":{}},\"stopPolicy\":\"{stop_policy}\",\"createdAt\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"specFolder\":\"{spec_folder}\"}'\n435:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n436: \n437:       step_create_findings_registry:\n438:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n439:         content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n440:         output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n441: \n442:       step_create_strategy:\n443:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n444:         template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n445:         populate:\n446:           review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n447:           review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n448:           dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n449:           scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n450:           cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n451:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n452:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n453:           stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n454:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n455: \n456:       step_seed_coverage_graph:\n457:         action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n458:         transform: |\n459:           1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n460:           2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n461:              or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n462:           3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n463:           4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n464:           5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n465:              returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n466:         bash: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n467:         outputs:\n468:           - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n469:           - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n470:           - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n471:         on_warning:\n472:           log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n473:           proceed: true\n474: \n475:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n476:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n477:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n478:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n479:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n480: \n481:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n482:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n483:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n484:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n485: \n486:       step_init_complete:\n487:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n488:         set: { current_iteration: 1, stuck_count: 0, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n489: \n490:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n491:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n492:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n493:   phase_loop:\n494:     purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n495:     repeat: true\n496:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n497:     steps:\n498: \n499:       step_read_state:\n500:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n501:         read:\n502:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n503:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n504:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n505:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n506:         extract:\n507:           - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n508:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n509:           - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n510:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n511:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n512:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n513:           - next_dimension: \"Next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md\"\n514:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n515:           - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n516:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n517:           - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n518:           - p0_count: \"Count P0 findings across all iterations\"\n519:           - p1_count: \"Count P1 findings across all iterations\"\n520:           - p2_count: \"Count P2 findings across all iterations\"\n521:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n522:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n523:           - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n524:           - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n525:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n526:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n527:           - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n528:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n529:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n530:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n531:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n532:           - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n533:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n534:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n535:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n536:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n537: \n538:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n539:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n540:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n541:         if_exists:\n542:           set:\n543:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n544:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n545:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n546:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n547:         if_not_exists:\n548:           proceed: true\n549: \n550:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n551:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n552:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n553:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n554:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n555: \n556:       step_graph_convergence:\n557:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline review convergence vote\"\n558:         inspect:\n559:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n560:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n561:         transform: |\n562:           1. Call graph convergence on the current review lineage before the inline 3-signal vote.\n563:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n564:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n565:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n566:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n567:         bash: 'node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\"'\n568:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Review-side graph convergence must run before the inline review stop vote.\"\n569:         append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n570:         outputs:\n571:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n572:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n573:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n574:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n575:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n576: \n577:       step_check_convergence:\n578:         action: \"Evaluate graph-assisted review stop conditions and the legal-stop decision tree\"\n579:         algorithm: |\n580:           0. CLAIM-ADJUDICATION PRE-CHECK (universal STOP veto; runs before hard stops and composite convergence):\n581:              claim_adjudication_gate_pass = (last_claim_adjudication_passed != false) OR (p0_count + p1_count == 0)\n582:              If claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false:\n583:                candidate_decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n584:                stop_blocked = true\n585:                stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n586:                blocked_gates = [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]\n587:                recovery_strategy = \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\"\n588:                Skip hard stops (1) and composite convergence (4); proceed directly to step 5 legal-stop decision-tree assembly so blocked_by_json, gate outputs, and the blocked_stop event still populate consistently.\n589:           1. HARD STOPS:\n590:              a) if iteration_count >= max_iterations: set decision = \"STOP\", stopReason = \"maxIterationsReached\", hard_stop_reason = \"max_iterations_reached\", preserve any failed legal-stop gates as terminal evidence, and proceed to synthesis without legal-stop veto\n591:              b) if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: do not allow all-dimensions-clean or composite convergence to stop; treat convergence signals as telemetry, set decision = \"CONTINUE\", and broaden the next review angle.\n592:              c) if all dimensions clean AND required traceability protocols are covered AND p0_count == 0 AND p1_count == 0 AND coverage_age >= 1 AND all quality gates pass (evidence: every P0/P1 has file:line; scope: all findings within target; coverage: all dimensions reviewed): mark hard_stop_reason = \"all_dimensions_clean\" and promote to STOP candidate\n593:              Operator stop reasons (`maxIterationsReached`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, unrecoverable `error`) are terminal ceilings. They do not hide failed gates; they record them in synthesis and stop dispatch.\n594:           2. STUCK DETECTION (threshold 2):\n595:              if stuck_count >= 2: STUCK_RECOVERY\n596:           3. GRAPH CONVERGENCE PREREQUISITE:\n597:                graph_decision, graph_signals_json, and graph_blockers_json are already populated by step_graph_convergence.\n598:                Final STOP is never legal unless the inline review vote says STOP AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\".\n599:                If graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\", set stop_blocked = true and route through blocked_stop emission instead of stopping.\n600:           4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n601:                signals = []\n602:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n603:                   avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n604:                   stop if avg <= 0.08\n605:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n606:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n607:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n608:                c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n609:                   coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n610:                   stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n611:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n612:                if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n613:                if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n614:                else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n615:           5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n616:                a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n617:                b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n618:                c) p0ResolutionGate: pass when activeP0 == 0; record activeP0\n619:                d) evidenceDensityGate: pass when every active P0/P1 has concrete file:line evidence and no active P0/P1 relies only on inference; record avgEvidencePerFinding\n620:                e) hotspotSaturationGate: pass when review hotspots have been revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic\n621:                f) claimAdjudicationGate: pass when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == true (i.e. last_claim_adjudication_passed != false OR there are no active P0/P1 findings to adjudicate); record last_claim_adjudication_passed and claim_adjudication_active_count\n622:                g) fixCompletenessReplayGate: pass when security_sensitive_fix_scope == false OR every required closed-gate replay row passes with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage; record security_sensitive_fix_scope, fix_completeness_replay_required_rows, and fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows\n623:                h) candidateCoverageGate: skip entirely when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 on the latest iteration. Otherwise pass when the current iteration's `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass` is `trivial` with `enforcement: \"skip\"` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` is non-empty, OR when the reducer registry's `searchDebt` is empty AND `candidateCoverage.covered` is a superset of `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` for the lineage. Otherwise pass = false; record `searchDebt` items as blocked-stop evidence; blocker name = \"candidateCoverageGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Resolve deferred/blocked obligations in next iteration or downgrade scope explicitly to trivial with cited evidence.\"\n624:              if STOP is a candidate and any gate fails:\n625:                decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n626:                stop_blocked = true\n627:                stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n628:                blocked_by_json = JSON array of failing gate names (always include \"claimAdjudicationGate\" when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false, \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\" when fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass == false, \"candidateCoverageGate\" when candidate_coverage_gate_pass == false, and \"graphlessFallbackGate\" when graphless_fallback_gate_pass == false)\n629:                blocked_by_csv = comma-separated list of failing gate names\n630:                convergence_gate_pass = boolean\n631:                convergence_gate_score = numeric convergence score\n632:                dimension_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n633:                dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = JSON array of covered review dimensions\n634:                dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = JSON array of missing review dimensions\n635:                p0_resolution_gate_pass = boolean\n636:                active_p0_count = number of active P0 findings\n637:                evidence_density_gate_pass = boolean\n638:                avg_evidence_per_finding = numeric evidence density\n639:                hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = boolean\n640:                claim_adjudication_gate_pass = boolean\n641:                claim_adjudication_active_count = numeric count of active P0/P1 at the gate\n642:                fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = boolean\n643:                security_sensitive_fix_scope = boolean\n644:                fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = numeric count of closed-gate replay rows required for security-sensitive fix reruns\n645:                fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = numeric count of required closed-gate replay rows marked PASS with evidence\n646:                candidate_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-646. Use offset=647 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_principles:","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: AUTONOMOUS DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nuser_inputs:\n  review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability] - Dimensions to check. Default: all.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n  session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime only persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive) and `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived). `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and no longer accepted — see deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n  max_iterations: 7\n  convergence_threshold: 0.10\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  mcp_integration:\n    tool: memory_context\n    note: \"Call MCP tools directly - NEVER through Code Mode\"\n    parameters: { input: \"{review_target}\", mode: \"focused\", intent: \"understand\", includeContent: true }\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".opencode/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: [mk-spec-memory]\n  tool_call_budget: { target: 9, soft_max: 12, hard_max: 13 }\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n    if_absent:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n\n  step_apply_lifecycle_request:\n    description: \"Honor explicit auto-mode restart before fan-out or normal initialization\"\n    skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n    instructions: |\n      This is the autonomous equivalent of the confirm-mode restart choice. Run it\n      immediately after artifact resolution and before fan-out so old packet files\n      cannot be merged with fresh lineage outputs. A restart request must never\n      fall back to auto-resume. In auto mode, the explicit restart flag is operator\n      authorization to archive the resolved review packet, so do not ask for a\n      second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped archive back to\n      the packet directory.\n    command: \"if [ -d \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" ]; then mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}\\\" && mv \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\\\"; fi; mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\"\"\n    outputs:\n      - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n      - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n    on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n\n  step_fanout_spawn:\n    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n    instructions: |\n      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n      A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n      session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n      self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n      first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n      deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n      deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n      sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n    sub_steps:\n      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n        description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n        command: |\n          node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n            --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n            --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n            --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n            --stop-policy {stop_policy}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n        detect:\n          canonical_review_state:\n            - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          legacy_review_state:\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n            - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n          legacy_review_markers:\n            - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n            - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n        migrate_only:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n        on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n        on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, append a migration event to the canonical JSONL, and leave unrelated scratch files untouched.\"\n        on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir} && if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}; find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; ; [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}; [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}; if [ -e {state_paths.state_log} ]; then printf '%s\\n' '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"migration\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"review\\\",\\\"legacyArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-research-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-research-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-research-pause\\\"],\\\"canonicalArtifacts\\\":[\\\"deep-review-config.json\\\",\\\"deep-review-state.jsonl\\\",\\\".deep-review-pause\\\"],\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\\\"}' >> {state_paths.state_log}; fi; fi; find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\\\; 2>/dev/null || true\"\n\n      step_acquire_lock:\n        action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n        command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder}\"\n        on_acquire: \"Capture ownerPid from the JSON output and reuse it for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n        note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls; stale-lock override is confirm-only or explicit recovery-only.\"\n        # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n        on_halt:\n          action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n          applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\"]\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n        on_cancel:\n          action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n        on_workflow_exit:\n          action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n\n      step_classify_session:\n        action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        classify:\n          fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n          resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n          completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n          invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n        outputs:\n          - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n        lifecycle_routing:\n          - \"If lineage_mode == restart and session_state is resume or completed-session, execute on_restart before on_resume or on_completed_session.\"\n          - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n        on_resume:\n          log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          skip_to: phase_loop\n        on_restart:\n          action: \"Archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n          command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n          set:\n            lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n            parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n            generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          skip_to: step_create_config\n        note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n        on_completed_session:\n          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n        on_invalid_state:\n          halt: true\n          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n        on_fresh:\n          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n\n      step_scope_discovery:\n        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n        resolve:\n          spec-folder: |\n            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, checklist.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n            6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n          skill: |\n            1. Read SKILL.md from .opencode/skills/{skill_name}/\n            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n          agent: |\n            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .opencode/agents/)\n            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n          track: |\n            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n            2. For each: read spec.md + checklist.md\n            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n          files: |\n            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n            2. Validate all files exist\n            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n        outputs:\n          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n\n      step_order_dimensions:\n        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions\n          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n        outputs:\n          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n          - inventory_pass: true\n\n      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n        outputs:\n          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n        normalize: |\n          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n          Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.\n\n      step_resolve_session_id:\n        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n        if_present:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n        if_absent:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n\n      step_create_config:\n        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n        template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n        populate:\n          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n          mode: \"review\"\n          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n          parentSessionId: null\n          lineageMode: \"new\"\n          generation: 1\n          continuedFromRun: null\n          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n          crossReference:\n            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n          stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n          stuckThreshold: 2\n          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n          status: \"initialized\"\n          releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n          executionMode: \"auto\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n\n      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Initialize JSONL state log with config record including review fields and lineage metadata\"\n        note: \"Reuse review_dimensions_json from step_normalize_review_dimensions. Never re-normalize or wrap the raw template value.\"\n        # Same parsed --no-resource-map flag honored here so config and state_log agree from line 1.\n        content: '{\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"reviewTarget\":\"{review_target}\",\"reviewTargetType\":\"{review_target_type}\",\"reviewDimensions\":{review_dimensions_json},\"resource_map_present\":{resource_map_present},\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":{resource_map_emit}},\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"convergenceThreshold\":{convergence_threshold},\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"{convergence_mode}\",\"divergent\":{}},\"stopPolicy\":\"{stop_policy}\",\"createdAt\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"specFolder\":\"{spec_folder}\"}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_create_findings_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n        template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n        action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n          2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n             or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n          3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n          4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n          5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n             returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n        bash: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n        outputs:\n          - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n          - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n          - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n        on_warning:\n          log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_init_complete:\n        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n        set: { current_iteration: 1, stuck_count: 0, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_loop:\n    purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n    repeat: true\n    max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n    steps:\n\n      step_read_state:\n        action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n          - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n          - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n          - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n          - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n          - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n          - next_dimension: \"Next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n          - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n          - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n          - p0_count: \"Count P0 findings across all iterations\"\n          - p1_count: \"Count P1 findings across all iterations\"\n          - p2_count: \"Count P2 findings across all iterations\"\n          - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n          - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n          - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n          - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n          - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n          - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n          - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n          - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n          - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n          - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n          - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n          - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n          - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n          - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n          - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n\n      step_check_pause_sentinel:\n        action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n        check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n        if_exists:\n          set:\n            pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n            pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n            pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n          skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n        if_not_exists:\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_validate_convergence_config:\n        action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n        if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n          log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n\n      step_graph_convergence:\n        action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline review convergence vote\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Call graph convergence on the current review lineage before the inline 3-signal vote.\n          2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n          3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n          4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n          5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n        bash: 'node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\"'\n        note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Review-side graph convergence must run before the inline review stop vote.\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n        outputs:\n          - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n          - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n          - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n          - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n          - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Evaluate graph-assisted review stop conditions and the legal-stop decision tree\"\n        algorithm: |\n          0. CLAIM-ADJUDICATION PRE-CHECK (universal STOP veto; runs before hard stops and composite convergence):\n             claim_adjudication_gate_pass = (last_claim_adjudication_passed != false) OR (p0_count + p1_count == 0)\n             If claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false:\n               candidate_decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n               stop_blocked = true\n               stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n               blocked_gates = [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]\n               recovery_strategy = \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\"\n               Skip hard stops (1) and composite convergence (4); proceed directly to step 5 legal-stop decision-tree assembly so blocked_by_json, gate outputs, and the blocked_stop event still populate consistently.\n          1. HARD STOPS:\n             a) if iteration_count >= max_iterations: set decision = \"STOP\", stopReason = \"maxIterationsReached\", hard_stop_reason = \"max_iterations_reached\", preserve any failed legal-stop gates as terminal evidence, and proceed to synthesis without legal-stop veto\n             b) if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: do not allow all-dimensions-clean or composite convergence to stop; treat convergence signals as telemetry, set decision = \"CONTINUE\", and broaden the next review angle.\n             c) if all dimensions clean AND required traceability protocols are covered AND p0_count == 0 AND p1_count == 0 AND coverage_age >= 1 AND all quality gates pass (evidence: every P0/P1 has file:line; scope: all findings within target; coverage: all dimensions reviewed): mark hard_stop_reason = \"all_dimensions_clean\" and promote to STOP candidate\n             Operator stop reasons (`maxIterationsReached`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, unrecoverable `error`) are terminal ceilings. They do not hide failed gates; they record them in synthesis and stop dispatch.\n          2. STUCK DETECTION (threshold 2):\n             if stuck_count >= 2: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. GRAPH CONVERGENCE PREREQUISITE:\n               graph_decision, graph_signals_json, and graph_blockers_json are already populated by step_graph_convergence.\n               Final STOP is never legal unless the inline review vote says STOP AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\".\n               If graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\", set stop_blocked = true and route through blocked_stop emission instead of stopping.\n          4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n               signals = []\n               a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n                  avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n                  stop if avg <= 0.08\n               b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n                  noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n                  stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n               c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n                  coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n                  stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n               Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n               if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n               if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n               else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n          5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n               a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n               b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n               c) p0ResolutionGate: pass when activeP0 == 0; record activeP0\n               d) evidenceDensityGate: pass when every active P0/P1 has concrete file:line evidence and no active P0/P1 relies only on inference; record avgEvidencePerFinding\n               e) hotspotSaturationGate: pass when review hotspots have been revisited enough times to satisfy the saturation heuristic\n               f) claimAdjudicationGate: pass when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == true (i.e. last_claim_adjudication_passed != false OR there are no active P0/P1 findings to adjudicate); record last_claim_adjudication_passed and claim_adjudication_active_count\n               g) fixCompletenessReplayGate: pass when security_sensitive_fix_scope == false OR every required closed-gate replay row passes with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage; record security_sensitive_fix_scope, fix_completeness_replay_required_rows, and fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows\n               h) candidateCoverageGate: skip entirely when `reviewDepthSchemaVersion` is not 2 on the latest iteration. Otherwise pass when the current iteration's `reviewDepthApplicability.scopeClass` is `trivial` with `enforcement: \"skip\"` AND `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` is non-empty, OR when the reducer registry's `searchDebt` is empty AND `candidateCoverage.covered` is a superset of `searchCoverage.requiredBugClasses` for the lineage. Otherwise pass = false; record `searchDebt` items as blocked-stop evidence; blocker name = \"candidateCoverageGate\"; recovery_strategy = \"Resolve deferred/blocked obligations in next iteration or downgrade scope explicitly to trivial with cited evidence.\"\n             if STOP is a candidate and any gate fails:\n               decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n               stop_blocked = true\n               stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n               blocked_by_json = JSON array of failing gate names (always include \"claimAdjudicationGate\" when claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false, \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\" when fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass == false, \"candidateCoverageGate\" when candidate_coverage_gate_pass == false, and \"graphlessFallbackGate\" when graphless_fallback_gate_pass == false)\n               blocked_by_csv = comma-separated list of failing gate names\n               convergence_gate_pass = boolean\n               convergence_gate_score = numeric convergence score\n               dimension_coverage_gate_pass = boolean\n               dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = JSON array of covered review dimensions\n               dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = JSON array of missing review dimensions\n               p0_resolution_gate_pass = boolean\n               active_p0_count = number of active P0 findings\n               evidence_density_gate_pass = boolean\n               avg_evidence_per_finding = numeric evidence density\n               hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = boolean\n               claim_adjudication_gate_pass = boolean\n               claim_adjudication_active_count = numeric count of active P0/P1 at the gate\n               fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = boolean\n               security_sensitive_fix_scope = boolean\n               fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = numeric count of closed-gate replay rows required for security-sensitive fix reruns\n               fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = numeric count of required closed-gate replay rows marked PASS with evidence\n               candidate_coverage_gate_pass = boolean","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":646,"totalLines":647,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml","time":{"start":1786124680546,"end":1786124680556}},"id":"prt_fdd53bc8a001O6Nw8i1oWea13V","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd53ae51001j39l3BT9X77daz"}}
