{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786124843402,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_eRNZ7pRKFjA5pDFdXMYs3739","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. TOPIC\n\nReview: README migration audit (deepseek-flash lineage)\nReview target: specs/system-speckit/032-relocate-specs-folder/005-readme-migration-audit (spec-folder)\nThis phase audits every non-worktree README in the repo (including root README.md) for content logically stale after the specs-root topology flip: `specs/` is canonical, `.opencode/specs` is a compat symlink. 21+ files carry a literal `.opencode/specs` reference; beyond literals, prose/diagram staleness must be caught.\n\n---\n\n## 2. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 10\n- Convergence threshold: 0.10\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-flash-1786124587346-0du5cu, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-08-07T19:46:00Z\n- Stop policy: max-iterations (convergence is telemetry until iteration 10)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 6. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not a general documentation-quality pass (typos, formatting, unrelated broken links) beyond migration-correctness flagging.\n- Not auditing non-README docs (`references/*.md`, `SKILL.md` bodies, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `PUBLIC-RELEASE.md`).\n- Not auditing `.worktrees/*` (duplicated checkouts).\n- Not auditing historical spec-doc content under `specs/**` that legitimately describes the pre-flip topology.\n\n---\n\n## 7. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- `maxIterations` (10) reached -- hard stop, then synthesize.\n- Convergence votes (rolling avg, MAD, dimension coverage) are telemetry only under max-iterations policy; they broaden the next angle rather than stopping early.\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\nD1 Correctness -- audit the literal `.opencode/specs` hit files for factual staleness (do they correctly describe the symlink, or claim the old canonical layout?).\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: 21+ non-worktree READMEs with literal `.opencode/specs` hits (root `README.md` explicitly named), plus any README with logically-stale prose/diagrams describing the pre-flip layout.\n- Behavior claims to verify: `specs/` is canonical, `.opencode/specs -> ../specs` is a compat symlink (confirmed live). READMEs claiming `.opencode/specs` as the canonical spec location are stale.\n- Reuse/conventions: phase 8 of 003-migration-execution already fixed `AGENTS.md`, `PUBLIC-RELEASE.md`, CI; this phase mirrors that precedent for READMEs.\n- Review risks/gaps: 753 non-worktree READMEs is too large to read line-by-line; prioritization via the literal-hit list plus targeted directory-structure/architecture-diagram sections.\n- resource-map.md not present. Skipping coverage gate.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | Verify README claims match real topology |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No checklist.md exists (Level 1 folder); N/A-ish, verify task evidence |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is spec-folder, not a skill |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is spec-folder, not an agent |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | Check if any README references a feature catalog describing old layout |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook in scope |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/system-speckit/032-relocate-specs-folder/005-readme-migration-audit/review/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/system-speckit/032-relocate-specs-folder/005-readme-migration-audit/review/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-review-strategy.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-speckit/032-relocate-specs-folder/005-readme-migration-audit/review/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-review-strategy.md","time":{"start":1786124843382,"end":1786124843400}},"id":"prt_fdd560e8a001anMmEM3leGOISc","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd55ff20001IYa1OyBa5neQFY"}}
