l fallback beats Qwen3 sidecar for default promotion: +0.4 pp hit-rate, +0.004 MRR, +9832.7 ms p95 | HOLD | `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/003-embedder-testing-and-architecture/008-rerank-sidecar-arc/004-spec-memory-rerank-benchmark/` |\n| May 20, 2026 | [`benchmark-2026-05-20/`](./2026-05-20--run--unspecified/) | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (ADR-013) re-bench: 9/10 top-1 ID-match (regenerated fixture, Z_SCORE_THRESHOLD tuned 1.5 -> 1.3, shared harness, embedding_cache reset), median 1071 ms, p95 2627 ms | PASS, matches May 17 baseline at stricter top-1 | `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/003-embedder-testing-and-architecture/002-spec-memory-stack/016-reindex-populates-vec-memories-knn-table/` through `019-lineage-and-metadata-repair-runner/` |\n| May 17, 2026 | [`benchmark-2026-05-17/`](./2026-05-17--run--unspecified/) | `jina-embeddings-v3` + retrieval-rescue layer (9/10 cat-24/409) | SHIPPED (ADR-012) | `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/003-memory-and-causal-runtime/003-embedder-testing-and-architecture/002-spec-memory-stack/004-spec-memory-embedder-bake-off/` |\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== cursor README rel link resolve ===\"; ls \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/hooks/cursor/../../../../../../.opencode/specs/cli-external-orchestration/030-cli-cursor-creation/004-cursor-hook-adapter-layer/decision-record.md\" 2>&1 | head -2\necho \"\"\necho \"=== devin README rel links ===\"; ls \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/hooks/devin/../../../../../../.opencode/specs/cli-external-orchestration/029-cli-devin-revival/hook-testing-results.md\" 2>&1 | head -2\necho \"\"\necho \"=== deep-alignment benchmark spec folder exists? ===\"; ls -d \"specs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration\" 2>&1; ls -d \".opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration\" 2>&1\necho \"\"\necho \"=== sk-create-benchmark pointer target ===\"; rg -n 'opencode/specs' .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-benchmark/references/shared/README.md\necho \"\"\necho \"=== mcp-server benchmarks rel links ===\"; sed -n '46,52p' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/benchmarks/README.md","time":{"start":1786125104003,"end":1786125104006}},"id":"prt_fdd5a2ae9001hw3eJiGBKygaIm","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd59d6a4001U3ewJVtgYBz0XZ"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786125105805,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"id":"prt_fdd5a3a8a001v3mL6Ebu9VPEwW","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fdd59d6a4001U3ewJVtgYBz0XZ","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":208407,"input":503,"output":405,"reasoning":2059,"cache":{"write":0,"read":205440}},"cost":0.001335572}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1786125109838,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"id":"prt_fdd5a4a4c001pQ67ryea5ZWX2J","messageID":"msg_fdd5a3fe3001qXOt4lRC3XEk1k","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786125147478,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_Tp06NuXFLoDzACtnTdpZ5341","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== system-spec-kit README: does it mention canonical/symlink? ===\"; rg -n 'canonical|symlink|specs root|spec root|\\.opencode/specs' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md | head -20\necho \"\"\necho \"=== sk-design-md-generator README output path usage ===\"; sed -n '76,92p' .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/README.md\necho \"\"\necho \"=== commands/create and commands/memory txt (out of README.md scope, note only) ===\"; rg -n 'opencode/specs' .opencode/commands/create/README.txt .opencode/commands/memory/README.txt","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"=== system-spec-kit README: does it mention canonical/symlink? ===\n41:System Spec Kit captures every file-modifying conversation in a templated spec folder, indexed at one of four documentation levels matched to task complexity. A local SQLite store makes those decisions searchable across sessions through five fused retrieval channels. `/speckit:resume` rebuilds the active context from packet-local sources. `/memory:save` routes session updates into canonical documentation surfaces so the next session picks up where the last one stopped, on any model or tool.\n92:Continuity no longer writes to `[spec]/memory/*.md`. Use `/memory:save` to route updates into the canonical packet docs:\n106:The command updates the canonical continuity surfaces for the target folder, refreshes `description.json.lastUpdated` and rewrites the derived fields in `graph-metadata.json`. The `/memory:save 042-my-feature` shorthand does the same. Direct MCP `memory_save({ filePath })` indexes content only and returns a `metadataRefresh` advisory with `refreshed: false` when packet metadata should be regenerated through the save lane.\n114:The system resolves the requested folder first. For a phase parent it follows the valid `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer into the active child. It then compares folder-local `handover.md` and `_memory.continuity` freshness and falls back to the packet's canonical spec docs. It presents the current state, prior decisions, touched files and next steps before you start.\n128:  .opencode/specs/[project]/042-my-feature/\n186:  └─► generate-context.js updates canonical continuity surfaces\n267:The `/speckit:implement` and `/speckit:complete` commands plus the nested changelog workflow can write packet history into a local `changelog/` directory when the target is a packet root or a direct child phase, using the canonical root and phase naming rules. Packet-local changelogs are additive, not a replacement for `implementation-summary.md`.\n283:`create.sh` rejects `--path` values that traverse outside the repository with a clear error before any write. Set `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` when a strict workflow should run full validation immediately after scaffolding. A mkdir-based advisory lock protects `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` writes during canonical save so two parallel `/memory:save` calls for the same packet do not race.\n438:When intake is still needed, `/speckit:plan` and `/speckit:complete` use the shared intake contract from `references/workflows/intake-contract.md`. Downstream callers consume the returned `start_state` as the canonical intake enum.\n661:ls -la .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n662:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n663:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/upgrade-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ [target-level]\n701:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/calculate-completeness.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n702:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ --verbose\n725:A: Spec folders capture what happened in structured documentation. `generate-context.js` updates the packet's canonical continuity surfaces. `/speckit:resume` rebuilds the next session from those sources, comparing folder-local `handover.md` and `_memory.continuity` freshness before falling back to packet docs. The MCP server indexes those sources so deeper retrieval still works through `session_bootstrap()`, `memory_context()`, `memory_match_triggers()` and `memory_search()`. One side captures, the recovery surfaces retrieve.\n729:A: The store can index any markdown file, beyond spec folder contents. For implementation work the canonical continuity path is the spec folder itself. You can still save standalone memories with `memory_save`, but Gate 3 will still ask about a spec folder for file modifications.\n748:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/upgrade-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ 2\n846:| `.opencode/specs/` | all spec folders created by Spec Kit |\n\n=== sk-design-md-generator README output path usage ===\n\n**Step 2: Extract tokens from a live site.** Run this from the repo root, not from `backend/`. `extract.ts` refuses any `--output` that resolves inside the skill, so a relative spec-folder path resolves correctly only from the repo root.\n\n```bash\nnpx ts-node .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/backend/scripts/extract.ts https://stripe.com --fast --output .opencode/specs/<track>/<packet>/output\n# --fast crawls 5 pages at 8 concurrency. tokens.json is written to <--output>/.\n```\n\nSuccess means `tokens.json` exists under the output directory with the measured values.\n\n**Step 3: Write the v3 Style Reference `DESIGN.md`.** Read `references/design-md-format.md` and `references/writing-style-guide.md`. The value-bearing token sections (Colors, Spacing & Shapes, Surfaces, Quick Start) are pre-rendered by `backend/scripts/build-write-prompt.ts` (which runs `formatters-v3.ts` first). You author the prose sections, including `Tokens - Typography`, taking every value from those pre-rendered sections or the FACTS block, never typing a number by hand. Every hex, pixel, font-weight, shadow and radius still traces to `tokens.json`.\n\n**Step 4: Validate before claiming completion.** Run from the repo root with the full script path:\n\n```bash\nnpx ts-node .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/backend/scripts/validate.ts DESIGN.md .opencode/specs/<track>/<packet>/output/tokens.json\n```\n\n=== commands/create and commands/memory txt (out of README.md scope, note only) ===\n.opencode/commands/memory/README.txt:323:| Manage scan finds 0 files | No continuity sources found in expected directories | Check canonical spec docs under `.opencode/specs/` and constitutional rules under `.opencode/skills/*/constitutional/` |\n.opencode/commands/create/README.txt:160:/create:changelog .opencode/specs/01--system-spec-kit/042-memory-upgrade :auto\n","metadata":{"output":"=== system-spec-kit README: does it mention canonical/symlink? ===\n41:System Spec Kit captures every file-modifying conversation in a templated spec folder, indexed at one of four documentation levels matched to task complexity. A local SQLite store makes those decisions searchable across sessions through five fused retrieval channels. `/speckit:resume` rebuilds the active context from packet-local sources. `/memory:save` routes session updates into canonical documentation surfaces so the next session picks up where the last one stopped, on any model or tool.\n92:Continuity no longer writes to `[spec]/memory/*.md`. Use `/memory:save` to route updates into the canonical packet docs:\n106:The command updates the canonical continuity surfaces for the target folder, refreshes `description.json.lastUpdated` and rewrites the derived fields in `graph-metadata.json`. The `/memory:save 042-my-feature` shorthand does the same. Direct MCP `memory_save({ filePath })` indexes content only and returns a `metadataRefresh` advisory with `refreshed: false` when packet metadata should be regenerated through the save lane.\n114:The system resolves the requested folder first. For a phase parent it follows the valid `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer into the active child. It then compares folder-local `handover.md` and `_memory.continuity` freshness and falls back to the packet's canonical spec docs. It presents the current state, prior decisions, touched files and next steps before you start.\n128:  .opencode/specs/[project]/042-my-feature/\n186:  └─► generate-context.js updates canonical continuity surfaces\n267:The `/speckit:implement` and `/speckit:complete` commands plus the nested changelog workflow can write packet history into a local `changelog/` directory when the target is a packet root or a direct child phase, using the canonical root and phase naming rules. Packet-local changelogs are additive, not a replacement for `implementation-summary.md`.\n283:`create.sh` rejects `--path` values that traverse outside the repository with a clear error before any write. Set `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` when a strict workflow should run full validation immediately after scaffolding. A mkdir-based advisory lock protects `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` writes during canonical save so two parallel `/memory:save` calls for the same packet do not race.\n438:When intake is still needed, `/speckit:plan` and `/speckit:complete` use the shared intake contract from `references/workflows/intake-contract.md`. Downstream callers consume the returned `start_state` as the canonical intake enum.\n661:ls -la .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n662:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n663:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/upgrade-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ [target-level]\n701:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/calculate-completeness.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n702:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ --verbose\n725:A: Spec folders capture what happened in structured documentation. `generate-context.js` updates the packet's canonical continuity surfaces. `/speckit:resume` rebuilds the next session from those sources, comparing folder-local `handover.md` and `_memory.continuity` freshness before falling back to packet docs. The MCP server indexes those sources so deeper retrieval still works through `session_bootstrap()`, `memory_context()`, `memory_match_triggers()` and `memory_search()`. One side captures, the recovery surfaces retrieve.\n729:A: The store can index any markdown file, beyond spec folder contents. For implementation work the canonical continuity path is the spec folder itself. You can still save standalone memories with `memory_save`, but Gate 3 will still ask about a spec folder for file modifications.\n748:bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/upgrade-level.sh .opencode/specs/[project]/NNN-feature/ 2\n846:| `.opencode/specs/` | all spec folders created by Spec Kit |\n\n=== sk-design-md-generator README output path usage ===\n\n**Step 2: Extract tokens from a live site.** Run this from the repo root, not from `backend/`. `extract.ts` refuses any `--output` that resolves inside the skill, so a relative spec-folder path resolves correctly only from the repo root.\n\n```bash\nnpx ts-node .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/backend/scripts/extract.ts https://stripe.com --fast --output .opencode/specs/<track>/<packet>/output\n# --fast crawls 5 pages at 8 concurrency. tokens.json is written to <--output>/.\n```\n\nSuccess means `tokens.json` exists under the output directory with the measured values.\n\n**Step 3: Write the v3 Style Reference `DESIGN.md`.** Read `references/design-md-format.md` and `references/writing-style-guide.md`. The value-bearing token sections (Colors, Spacing & Shapes, Surfaces, Quick Start) are pre-rendered by `backend/scripts/build-write-prompt.ts` (which runs `formatters-v3.ts` first). You author the prose sections, including `Tokens - Typography`, taking every value from those pre-rendered sections or the FACTS block, never typing a number by hand. Every hex, pixel, font-weight, shadow and radius still traces to `tokens.json`.\n\n**Step 4: Validate before claiming completion.** Run from the repo root with the full script path:\n\n```bash\nnpx ts-node .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/backend/scripts/validate.ts DESIGN.md .opencode/specs/<track>/<packet>/output/tokens.json\n```\n\n=== commands/create and commands/memory txt (out of README.md scope, note only) ===\n.opencode/commands/memory/README.txt:323:| Manage scan finds 0 files | No continuity sources found in expected directories | Check canonical spec docs under `.opencode/specs/` and constitutional rules under `.opencode/skills/*/constitutional/` |\n.opencode/commands/create/README.txt:160:/create:changelog .opencode/specs/01--system-spec-kit/042-memory-upgrade :auto\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== system-spec-kit README: does it mention canonical/symlink? ===\"; rg -n 'canonical|symlink|specs root|spec root|\\.opencode/specs' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md | head -20\necho \"\"\necho \"=== sk-design-md-generator README output path usage ===\"; sed -n '76,92p' .opencode/skills/sk-design/sk-design-md-generator/README.md\necho \"\"\necho \"=== commands/create and commands/memory txt (out of README.md scope, note only) ===\"; rg -n 'opencode/specs' .opencode/commands/create/README.txt .opencode/commands/memory/README.txt","time":{"start":1786125147470,"end":1786125147477}},"id":"prt_fdd5ad85a001deGMRQb0eVaTq5","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd5a3fe3001qXOt4lRC3XEk1k"}}
