{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786125806789,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_diqs1mKeEimXtBG1bT3k0620","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== system-spec-kit/scripts/README.md prose ===\"\nrg -n 'specs|spec' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/README.md | head -10\necho \"\"\necho \"=== spec.md:105 claim 'plan.md names the exact command' - is that true? ===\"\necho \"plan.md mentions any command?\"\nrg -n 'rg |grep |census|command' specs/system-speckit/032-relocate-specs-folder/005-readme-migration-audit/plan.md | head","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"=== system-spec-kit/scripts/README.md prose ===\n3:description: \"Script package entrypoints, source zones, boundaries and validation commands for system-spec-kit.\"\n5:  - \"spec kit scripts\"\n17:`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/` contains the shell and TypeScript tooling for spec lifecycle work, memory saves, metadata refresh, evaluations, setup checks and script regression coverage.\n21:- Shell entrypoints live in focused folders such as `spec/`, `rules/`, `setup/` and `ops/`.\n36:│ or command   │      │ spec, memory   │      │ or graph files  │\n60:+-- spec/                  # Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints\n66:+-- spec-folder/           # Spec folder metadata and detection modules\n98:- Shared helpers should not own spec folder policy that belongs in `spec/` or `rules/`.\n107:| `spec/` | Creates, upgrades, validates, completes and archives spec folders. |\n108:| `rules/` | Holds validation checks used by `spec/validate.sh`. |\n\n=== spec.md:105 claim 'plan.md names the exact command' - is that true? ===\nplan.md mentions any command?\n41:| **Framework** | `/deep:review` via the `system-deep-loop` skill (Claude Code entry point for the OpenCode-native `.opencode/commands/deep/review.md` workflow) |\n55:- [x] Real README census run (753 non-worktree files,