{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786126133070,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_ET_94NftnCnbYpYKRwZHRlP1971","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== Maintainability: internal consistency of system-spec-kit README — does templates/README already use canonical specs/ while main README uses legacy? ===\"\necho \"templates/README canonical usage (positive control): lines 69, 180, 202, 237 use specs/\"\necho \"main README legacy usage: lines 128, 661-663, 701-702, 748, 846 use .opencode/specs\"\necho \"\"\necho \"=== mcp-server hooks README (index) — does it mention specs root? ===\"\nrg -n 'specs' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/hooks/README.md | head -5\necho \"\"\necho \"=== any duplicate README pairs (e.g. scripts/git-hooks README vs repo git-hooks README) describing same thing inconsistently? ===\"\necho \"--- repo-level scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28,37 (drift marker) ---\"\necho \"--- skill-level scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3,18 (drift marker) ---\"\necho \"both describe drift-marker-write.ts; check wording consistency:\"\nrg -n 'opencode/specs' .opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md | head","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"=== Maintainability: internal consistency of system-spec-kit README — does templates/README already use canonical specs/ while main README uses legacy? ===\ntemplates/README canonical usage (positive control): lines 69, 180, 202, 237 use specs/\nmain README legacy usage: lines 128, 661-663, 701-702, 748, 846 use .opencode/specs\n\n=== mcp-server hooks README (index) — does it mention specs root? ===\n\n=== any duplicate README pairs (e.g. scripts/git-hooks README vs repo git-hooks README) describing same thing inconsistently? ===\n--- repo-level scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28,37 (drift marker) ---\n--- skill-level scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3,18 (drift marker) ---\nboth describe drift-marker-write.ts; check wording consistency:\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3:description: \"TypeScript source for the drift marker that git lifecycle hooks write after a rename or delete under .opencode/specs.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md:18:| `drift-marker-write.ts` | Reads `MEMORY_DRIFT_DIFF` and `MEMORY_DRIFT_REPO_ROOT` from the environment, parses renamed and deleted `.opencode/specs` paths out of a `git diff-tree --name-status` diff and merges them into a lock-guarded, atomically written drift-marker JSON file so the memory index can reconcile stale paths. |\n.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28:| [`memory-drift-marker.sh`](memory-drift-marker.sh) | Diffs commit ranges for changes under `.opencode/specs` and passes matching rename or deletion data to the built drift-marker writer. |\n.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:37:| `memory-drift-marker.sh` | `mark_memory_drift_from_diff()` collects `.opencode/specs` changes with `git diff-tree` and invokes `drift-marker-write.js`. It skips work when no relevant diff, Node.js or built writer exists. | [`post-commit`](../post-commit), [`post-merge`](../post-merge) and [`post-rewrite`](../post-rewrite) |\n","metadata":{"output":"=== Maintainability: internal consistency of system-spec-kit README — does templates/README already use canonical specs/ while main README uses legacy? ===\ntemplates/README canonical usage (positive control): lines 69, 180, 202, 237 use specs/\nmain README legacy usage: lines 128, 661-663, 701-702, 748, 846 use .opencode/specs\n\n=== mcp-server hooks README (index) — does it mention specs root? ===\n\n=== any duplicate README pairs (e.g. scripts/git-hooks README vs repo git-hooks README) describing same thing inconsistently? ===\n--- repo-level scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28,37 (drift marker) ---\n--- skill-level scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3,18 (drift marker) ---\nboth describe drift-marker-write.ts; check wording consistency:\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3:description: \"TypeScript source for the drift marker that git lifecycle hooks write after a rename or delete under .opencode/specs.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md:18:| `drift-marker-write.ts` | Reads `MEMORY_DRIFT_DIFF` and `MEMORY_DRIFT_REPO_ROOT` from the environment, parses renamed and deleted `.opencode/specs` paths out of a `git diff-tree --name-status` diff and merges them into a lock-guarded, atomically written drift-marker JSON file so the memory index can reconcile stale paths. |\n.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28:| [`memory-drift-marker.sh`](memory-drift-marker.sh) | Diffs commit ranges for changes under `.opencode/specs` and passes matching rename or deletion data to the built drift-marker writer. |\n.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:37:| `memory-drift-marker.sh` | `mark_memory_drift_from_diff()` collects `.opencode/specs` changes with `git diff-tree` and invokes `drift-marker-write.js`. It skips work when no relevant diff, Node.js or built writer exists. | [`post-commit`](../post-commit), [`post-merge`](../post-merge) and [`post-rewrite`](../post-rewrite) |\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== Maintainability: internal consistency of system-spec-kit README — does templates/README already use canonical specs/ while main README uses legacy? ===\"\necho \"templates/README canonical usage (positive control): lines 69, 180, 202, 237 use specs/\"\necho \"main README legacy usage: lines 128, 661-663, 701-702, 748, 846 use .opencode/specs\"\necho \"\"\necho \"=== mcp-server hooks README (index) — does it mention specs root? ===\"\nrg -n 'specs' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/hooks/README.md | head -5\necho \"\"\necho \"=== any duplicate README pairs (e.g. scripts/git-hooks README vs repo git-hooks README) describing same thing inconsistently? ===\"\necho \"--- repo-level scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md:28,37 (drift marker) ---\"\necho \"--- skill-level scripts/git-hooks/README.md:3,18 (drift marker) ---\"\necho \"both describe drift-marker-write.ts; check wording consistency:\"\nrg -n 'opencode/specs' .opencode/scripts/git-hooks/lib/README.md .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/git-hooks/README.md | head","time":{"start":1786126133066,"end":1786126133069}},"id":"prt_fdd69dd750015K2CcWpAnlEpZh","sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","messageID":"msg_fdd69cf70001SRe3Yn9ectAgir"}}
