{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786126247363,"sessionID":"ses_022ada93cffeiuPDQc9GVcDNCF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_7gKcleVJFFElBenWJMdn5627","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== robust correct-as-is check: any live (non-specs) README line mentioning both specs and symlink/alias/canonical? ===\"\nrg -n 'symlink|compat|canonical' -g 'README.md' -g '!**/.worktrees/**' -g '!**/node_modules/**' -g '!specs/**' .opencode 2>/dev/null | rg 'specs|spec ' | head -8\necho \"=> (empty means none)\"\necho \"\"\necho \"=== confirm z_archive historical README is the only alias-roots mention ===\"\nrg -ln 'alias roots|both `specs/` and' -g 'README.md' -g '!**/.worktrees/**' -g '!**/node_modules/**' . 2>/dev/null | head -5\necho \"\"\necho \"=== deep-alignment line 34 target exists at canonical specs/ ? ===\"\nls -d specs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/ 2>&1 | head -1\nls -d specs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration 2>&1 | head -1","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public"},"output":"=== robust correct-as-is check: any live (non-specs) README line mentioning both specs and symlink/alias/canonical? ===\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/scratch/README.md:20:- Permanent context belongs in canonical spec documents.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md:30:`templates/changelog/` contains packet-local changelog templates generated inside spec folders. These templates summarize canonical packet docs and are separate from global release-note templates under `.opencode/changelog/`.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md:81:│ canonical spec docs│\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/session/README.md:23:- Session state supports `/speckit:resume`, but the canonical recovery ladder remains `handover.md` → `_memory.continuity` → spec docs.\n.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-quality-control/README.md:121:A: The packet escalates instead of editing. Product claims and policy text, plus canonical spec decisions, need a human decision, not a quality-pass rewrite.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/utils/README.md:105:| `scratch/`, `temp/`, `research/iterations/`, `review/iterations/` | spec-doc scope-excluded | Working artifacts and iteration outputs are not classified as canonical spec documents, so they are absent from spec-doc retrieval rather than merely downweighted. |\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/resume/README.md:15:- `resume-ladder.ts` resolves the active spec folder, follows a phase parent's `derived.last_active_child_id` to a valid child when present, and rebuilds packet continuity from `handover.md`, then `_memory.continuity`, then the canonical spec docs.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/README.md:58:- `test-fixtures` symlink for shared spec folder validation cases.\n=> (empty means none)\n\n=== confirm z_archive historical README is the only alias-roots mention ===\n./specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/022-sk-deep-research-evolution/006-sk-deep-research-review-folders/README.md\n\n=== deep-alignment line 34 target exists at canonical specs/ ? ===\nspecs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/\nspecs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration\n","metadata":{"output":"=== robust correct-as-is check: any live (non-specs) README line mentioning both specs and symlink/alias/canonical? ===\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/scratch/README.md:20:- Permanent context belongs in canonical spec documents.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md:30:`templates/changelog/` contains packet-local changelog templates generated inside spec folders. These templates summarize canonical packet docs and are separate from global release-note templates under `.opencode/changelog/`.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md:81:│ canonical spec docs│\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/session/README.md:23:- Session state supports `/speckit:resume`, but the canonical recovery ladder remains `handover.md` → `_memory.continuity` → spec docs.\n.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-quality-control/README.md:121:A: The packet escalates instead of editing. Product claims and policy text, plus canonical spec decisions, need a human decision, not a quality-pass rewrite.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/utils/README.md:105:| `scratch/`, `temp/`, `research/iterations/`, `review/iterations/` | spec-doc scope-excluded | Working artifacts and iteration outputs are not classified as canonical spec documents, so they are absent from spec-doc retrieval rather than merely downweighted. |\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/lib/resume/README.md:15:- `resume-ladder.ts` resolves the active spec folder, follows a phase parent's `derived.last_active_child_id` to a valid child when present, and rebuilds packet continuity from `handover.md`, then `_memory.continuity`, then the canonical spec docs.\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/README.md:58:- `test-fixtures` symlink for shared spec folder validation cases.\n=> (empty means none)\n\n=== confirm z_archive historical README is the only alias-roots mention ===\n./specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/022-sk-deep-research-evolution/006-sk-deep-research-review-folders/README.md\n\n=== deep-alignment line 34 target exists at canonical specs/ ? ===\nspecs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/\nspecs/system-deep-loop/035-command-surface-benchmark/004-command-lane-integration\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== robust correct-as-is check: any live (non-specs) README line mentioning both specs and symlink/alias/canonical? ===\"\nrg -n 'symlink|compat|canonical' -g 'README.md' -g '!**/.worktrees/**' -g '!**/node_modules/**' -g '!specs/**' .opencode 2>/dev/null | rg 'specs|spec ' | head -8\necho \"=